ertaken a huge number of renovation projects, which no doubt everyone within the city limits has noticed."vTell us, after being trapped in time for more than a decade, what inspired you to take on this enormous workload?"AADRIENN: When I grew up-- or rather, in the time I grew up--"5This whole time distortion thing is confusing..."eBack then, Reborn was a region renowned for its beauty, and the city matched that acre for acre."\Since I came back, I've seen so many ways how Reborn City is just not what it once was.""It's shocking-- painful even."KSo, it's only natural that I'm going to do everything I can to fix it."NGARDEVOIR: Well said! Aren't you cute, always playing the good samaritan!"%"I will protect you, Gardevoir!""1ADRIENN: Ahaha, can't we let that go by now?"GARDEVOIR: Nope!"6"I will restore the city!" It's adorable, really!"KADRIENN: Do I really sound like that? You're starting to embarrass me.".GARDEVOIR: Good! That's my job, you know?".ADRIENN: No, I um, didn't know, actually."+I thought this was a formal interview?"&GARDEVOIR: It is! It's so formal!"It's the formal-est!"3There hasn't been a more formal interview yet!"BADRIENN: Based on the ones I've seen, I would believe that..."4GARDEVOIR: What? What's that supposed to mean?!"LNow listen here, before you go saying that, let me explain you a thing!"Wait, first... Cut, cut!"NToday we have a special report with Gym Leader Florinia of the Onyx Ward!"fMany Trainers are well-acquainted with Florinia as the headmistress of the Onyx Trainers' School."cTell us, Florinia, how exactly did you manage to secure a position so prestigious at your age?"lFLORINIA: Principality of the school was requested following the acceptance of the Gym Leader position."{The conversion of city-public property was acknowledged as necessary to be forfeit for the foundation of the Reborn League,"=Thus, what was once solely a school became solely a Gym."lUpon gaining control of the facility, and proper permissions following, the institution was hybridized."KGARDEVOIR: I see! So in other words, it was your idea to combine them!"WYou must have a real passion for education to be willing to take that on yourself!"/FLORINIA: Passion is an irrelevant factor."QThe operation is necessary, and this speaker is able to function adequately."<GARDEVOIR: Oh? Does that mean you don't enjoy the work?")FLORINIA: Enjoyment is a triviality."Only function matters."GARDEVOIR: How boring!">Surely there must be something you enjoy doing, Florinia?"bFLORINIA: Personal emotion is too confounding of a condition to reach that assumption safely."DAnd misinterpretation of human emotion can lead to severe risk."iThis writer has already lost too much at its hand; thus, as logically directed, the risk is avoided."%GARDEVOIR: Oh my, this is juicy!"vSo you were hurt by someone in the past and that's why you ignore your emotions-- is that what I'm understanding?"1FLORINIA: That is a sufficent abstract, yes."/GARDEVOIR: Lovely! Do tell, what happened?"6FLORINIA: The conclusion will not be forthcoming.")The previous analysis is sufficient."Good bye."=GARDEVOIR: What? I say when the interview ends, not you!",Darn it! This was finally getting good!"CI'm here right now with someone very special to me personally."JSay hello to Reborn's Ice Gym Leader and former model, Serra Voclain!"4SERRA: Goodness, Gardevoir, this is a surprise."MI assumed you'd come back home to collect your belongings, not for this."@GARDEVOIR: What's the matter? You seem almost disappointed!"!SERRA: No, not in the least."DNeither by the interview nor by you not collecting your things."1Lord knows no one else is using those rooms."BIt's just been a long time since I've had a public interview."-It's not a feeling I'd expected to miss."dGARDEVOIR: That's right, you gave up your career for your son before. Do you regret doing that?"SERRA: It's hard to say."ÅI think the best way to put it is-- although I do feel remorse for what I've lost, I wouldn't change my decision even if I could."?There are more important things than passions and careers.";GARDEVOIR: You mean your son, of course. How touching!"But, tell me, how do you respond to the recent developments wherein he's fallen in with the terrorist organization Team Meteor?"SERRA: I'm sorry."He's what?"~GARDEVOIR: In his recent exploits, it seems likely he's been working under and assisting Team Meteor in destroying the region!"SERRA: He's--"&...Gardevoir, take me to Bennett."BGARDEVOIR: Ah, in time, but let's finish the interview first?"SERRA: Gardevoir."Take me to Bennett."GARDEVOIR: ...Yes, missus."mI'm here today at the homestead and gymstead of one of Reborn's most popular Trainers, Ms. Amaria Fiore!"ÄUnfortunately, and in a surprise twist for our Interview Intermission, Amaria is actually not available for comment right now..."9...seeing as she is currently setting up for battle!"êThere's been quite a lot going on in this bubbly beauty's life, but luckily, your truest friend, Gossip Gardevoir, is here to catch up to speed."èSee, after a recent accident of questionably self- inflicted causes, Ms. Fiore here has developed a sudden textbook case of retrograde amnesia,"ëAnd as such has forgotten everything that's occurred in recent events, including things that should have been precious to her and her loved ones."ÑThe battle that's taking place today is not between her and a challenger, but between her and a representative of the Reborn League,"QTo assess if she is still able to retain her position despite her condition!"¶Everything is on the line for Amaria today! If it proves that her battling ability went down the drain with her memory, she could find herself out of a job in a snap!">Let's cut to the battlefield now and see how she's doing!">Oh, there's nothing happening? Have they not started yet?"1...What do you mean, they already finished!?"AI was still giving the intro! What kind of battle was that?!"O-oh. I... I see."Well, folks,"PIn a turn of events that is at once altogether unsurprising yet unexpected,"}In the time it took me to preface the battle, Amaria has already beaten her opponent for a flawless six-zero shutout victory!"~Gotta hand it to the woman of the water, she sure knows how to cling onto her talent even when she loses everything else!"jAnd that, my dear viewers, is exactly proof as to why she is one of Reborn's most famous Gym Leaders!"RToday we're meeting Julia Wilde in a quaint cafe to get a bite-- and a scoop."Here she comes now--"XShe strolls through the door, swag in every step and saffron seifuku in full bloom,"_She rocks a pair of shades like it's nobody's business and they just have to deal with it."HThe girl's got style, the girl's got class, she's coming this way--"...And she crashed."$Julia, helloooo? I'm over here!"JULIA: Huh..."OGARDEVOIR: Just where were you looking?! You walked right into that table!"!JULIA: Oh... Good morning..."zGARDEVOIR: Wait, were you wearing those shades just to hide the fact that your eyes were closed as you were walking?!"OJULIA: Well, duh... How else am I gonna sleepwalk without anyone noticing?"JGARDEVOIR: I'm not so sure that's quite how sleepwalking works, dear."2JULIA: Hey, who's the expert here? You or me?"2I don't see you sleepwalking into any tables!"GARDEVOIR: As if I would!"ASo much for class... Go on, pick up that chair and sit down."TSo, Julia, I understand you have somewhat of a fixation with blowing things up."JULIA: It's just a hobby!"7GARDEVOIR: Could you tell us how that got started?"JULIA: Yeah!"éOkay, so, when I was younger, I dated this guy named Rod-- actually, was it Rod? Maybe that was Ringo... I always get them mixed up. Anyways--"óSo, we were out at the park this one time and he keeps like, checking his phone, right? So, at one point he steps into the restroom and I check it too,"çTo like, see what was so important that he was taking time away from me-- anyway, it turned out he was texting this other girl, and you know,"QThere's really only one logical thing to do in a situation like that, right?"üWhich is to open up his phone and change around a couple wires and have a Pok√©mon jolt up the battery, just to make it glitch out, give a little spook, right?")I mean, that's what anyone would do."So, he gets back from the bathroom and starts up the phone and he doesn't expect a thing, but I'm just sitting there like ":3c""~And then, suddenly the whole device sparks and the screen melts and he screams and throws it away and it hits a wall and BOOM!")I hadn't felt that excited in years!"7Like, blowing things up is WAY more fun than guys."2But if you COMBINE the two, it's even better!"hNot that I'm trying to blow any guys up... But you know, the look on their faces is just priceless!""GARDEVOIR: I'm... sure it is."6Listen, have you considered professional therapy?"JULIA: Therapy? Me?"hOh, no, I'm not really good at giving advice and helping people. I'm flattered you think so though!"BAnyway, I thought the whole kaboom-thing might come up today,"#So I prepared a demonstration!"Do you wanna see?"GARDEVOIR: NO."-beep-"GARDEVOIR: Uh."qToday I'm here in Calcenon City to interview the smoldering beauty famed for the flames-- Charlotte Belrose!"?Charlotte, thanks for taking the time to talk to me today."ICHARLOTTE: Sure thing, Gardevoir. In fact, I should be thanking you."PWe're in ground zero and things are about as boring as they can be up here."^It's always a pleasure to take some time out of my day to embarrass someone on public TV."1GARDEVOIR: That's-- No, wait, that's my job.",CHARLOTTE: By 'someone' I meant myself."=GARDEVOIR: Oh! Well, no need to be embarrassed, darling."5I must admit, you didn't seem like the shy type."CHARLOTTE: I'm not."GARDEVOIR: Well-- okay."=Whatever the case, don't worry, I'm sure you'll do fine!"'CHARLOTTE: I'm not worried either."5I wasn't even serious about embarrassing myself."_But it's nice that you try and think of the comfort levels of your guests once in a while."nGARDEVOIR: Of course! That's just what a good hostess should-- Wait, what do you mean, "Once in a while"?"/CHARLOTTE: I've seen your past interviews."SYou normally just act all high and mighty while you put someone else on blast."Am I wrong?"'GARDEVOIR: Of course you're wrong!"gCHARLOTTE: That's funny, because I distinctly remember you tearing into Aya in a previous episode.":Threatening to tell the world about her relationship?",That doesn't seem very courteous to me."&GARDEVOIR: She called the police!"3CHARLOTTE: You're right, that was rude of her."AAlmost as rude as you being in her house without permission."EGARDEVOIR: And still not half as rude as you're being right now!"!CHARLOTTE: Oh, you're right."ÖMy apologies, Gardevoir, I thought that you would be more supportive of your fans who've watched so many of your past TV appearances."9I guess this is just how much we mean to you though."0GARDEVOIR: That's not what I'm saying! Ugh!"fCHARLOTTE: You've got such a short fuse. Do you really get along well with the sponsors this way?"-GARDEVOIR: That's none of your business!"1CHARLOTTE: Do you want to know what I think?"I think you're lying."GARDEVOIR: Lying?""Okay, sure, this sounds good."'Tell me, almighty, wise Charlotte."What am I lying about?")CHARLOTTE: You're lying to yourself."6You know the truth about why this show is funded."%It's because you're a character."LGARDEVOIR: A character? Like in a game or something? That's ridiculous."^CHARLOTTE: You're sold to the public masses as a foolish, incompetent reporter character."CThe only value in these interviews comes from your buffoonery."(Why else wouldn't it be edited out?"GBut you have this egocentric streak that lashes back when prodded."JIf you were really playing a character, you wouldn't be so sensitive."YYou'd have an understanding that the you on TV is different than who you really are."But you don't."IBecause you're every bit as impulsive and incompetent as you appear."But the worst part is,".You won't admit it even when you know it."`Even if you're impulsive, you're not so stupid as to not have thought about your own shows."ãYou realized that you were just being used and made fun of, but you wanted to believe you were actually a famous person people cared about."OSo you've been playing make-believe with your own success this whole time.""GARDEVOIR: That's nonsense..."CHARLOTTE: Is it?"/Look me in the eyes and tell me I'm wrong."8We're here today with one of Reborn's Elite Four..."She's powerful..."She's ferocious..."AAnd she's four feet and three inches of pure battling skill!"'Let's hear it for Heather Molinar!"8Heather, thanks so much for joining us on the show!".HEATHER: Thanks for having me, Gardevoir!"KIt's a nice change for someone to recognize strength when they see it!"CGARDEVOIR: Those are some mighty words for such a tiny person!"GBut certainly your status threatens to back those words up nicely.">Can you tell us where you think your strength comes from?"9HEATHER: Well, obviously, it comes from my Pok√©mon."And..."I guess, my friends too."5GARDEVOIR: Your friends? Whoever could you mean?"fHEATHER: Well, there were a couple Trainers who wanted to help me out after I ran away from home.""Cain, even though he's weird."+And \PN keeps showing up everywhere..."HEven I know things wouldn't have worked out this well without them."But mostly..."I mean my friend, Shelly."IWe met after I got mad at my dad and took off for a few days before."FShe hid me in her Gym and we had a lot of fun playing together..."Well, I had fun, at least.".I guess we just always did what I wanted.";But she was there to help me after things got bad too."3I guess she liked me too, for whatever reason.""I don't really get it, but...",I wanna try and make it back up to her."1She was really nice to me and I was selfish."2So I gotta be a good friend from now on, too."HGARDEVOIR: Admirable words from someone who's been through so much!"KIt seems like this young Trainer has really found the resolve to grow!"GI wonder what that could mean for the future of this battler, too!"cAny certain Trainers out there looking to face the Elite Four soon may just want to watch out!"DHEATHER: Obviously! It's just cuz I'm the princess of the wind!">GARDEVOIR: The princess of the wind? However do you mean?"ZHEATHER: My Mom was a Flying-type Trainer too, so that's kind of like being the wind!"`I learned what I could from how she used to battle, and now I'm even stronger than she was!";GARDEVOIR: Oh my, even stronger? That's quite a claim!"PHEATHER: But it's true! Cuz she only used Pok√©mon she thought were cute..."Like Salamence!"_Okay, so it's not exactly the usual "cute"-- but that shouldn't be the determining factor!"IAs a top tier battler, I'm not afraid to use the big, powerful ones!"XEveryone's always like "Whaaat? Why would a little girl want a Pok√©mon like that?""oAnd they try to pass me off with Buneary or Pikachu or some other crap Fairy trash just because it's pink.""Who cares about any of that?!"4I don't need to look cute, I need to kick butt!"*And that's exactly what I'm gonna do!"1GARDEVOIR: That's quite the fighting spirit!"uAnd there you have it, folks-- a girl who's not afraid to take on the whole world with the help of her Pok√©mon!"UI feel sorry for whatever stray challenger ends up opposite to her in the arena!"4That's all on today's Interview Intermission..."CThat's all on today's Interview Intermission. Until next time!"|Yo, Reborn City! What's up?! We're here with the Reborn Rundown, giving you a look at the Leaders of the Reborn League!",I'm your host, DJ Arclight, now on air!"5Let's talk about Julia, the Peridot Ward Leader."uJulia's a bombastic battling babe bursting onto the scene after having graduated from the Onyx Trainers' School."{With a history of leading Pok√©mon and cheerleading teams alike, any challenger is promised an exciting battle against her!"}Her Electric-types fall right in line with this, beating down her competitors with a barrage of her signature "boomies"."ãSonic Boom and Explosion attacks form the chorus of her routine, so any Trainers planning to take her on should be ready to take some hits!"~Take particular care with her Electrode, whose lightning-fast Speed and set damage takes the battle to a crescendo in a blink!"qLet's have a quick review of Head Instructor Florinia, Leader of the Onyx Trainers' School in the Onyx Ward."Take notes!"TLike any good principal, Florinia takes education and knowledge very seriously."ÇHer fighting style makes use of both weather and terrain to overwhelm her opponents in stall-tactics with residual damage effects."ONot only that, but her signature move, Nature Power, takes a brain to use."~Most Trainers know that the attack changes based on the environment, but can you match your moves to the field you're on?"VYou'll certainly need a tactical advantage to take on her star Pok√©mon, Cradily!"öTaking center stage in her 'desert rose' fighting style, a Mono-Grass Sandstorm hybrid, Cradily requires either pure strength or pure cunning to take out."bToday, we're going to be taking a break from our usual programming to dive into some history!"gSpecifically, we'll be looking at the now-retired Poison Gym Leader of an era past, Corey Molinar!"{An older man with more derision than a grandma at a metal show, this former star pours it on thick with the pessimism."«Not a whole lot is known about the man except that he appears to have some training as a pharmacist, and works in cooperation with Reborn City police supplying valuable forensic chemicals and advice."ùHere's a scoop though-- some residents of the Beryl Ward, where he's known to live, report him frequently visiting and spending hours at the nearby cemetery!"But who could that be for?"Even I'm not sure."=If you ask me, someone oughta go smack a smile into him.">Life's too short to be moping around all the time, yanno?"^Trainers, should you find yourself in a chance battle against the old Leader, be careful!"IHis Crobat is a speed demon, and its attacks are no laughing matter."eTake special care not to let it set up by keeping pressure on it with status moves or hard-hits."CPerseverance will always win the day in the face of pessimism!"7Let's talk about Shelly, Leader of the Lapis Ward!"AShe's a timid soul with a passion for reading and knowledge."`In fact, it's rare to see the girl without her nose in a book, but it's paid off in spades."lAll that studying means that she knows just what kind of tune to have her Bug-types play in any battle!"jShelly herself prefers Double Battles, using rain to cover her weaknesses and overwhelm the opponent."nHer signature Pok√©mon, Illumise and Volbeat, are the prelude and finale each to her tactical advantages,"USo if you find yourself facing the bookworm, focus down her supports right away!";We've got some sort of mystery for you today, viewers."2Let's talk about Shade, the Ghost Gym Leader."kMost people aren't all that sure if Shade is human, a ghost himself, or maybe something else entirely!"åGiven that he rarely speaks, and that when he does, he seldom makes common sense, there's not a whole lot we can tell you about this entity."7In battle, look out for his ace Pok√©mon, Mimikyu!"õThat Pok√©mon hides nearly as much as the Leader himself does, but rather than a sinister smile to top it all off, Mimikyu's Disguise makes it hard to hit."?Do your best not to let it get the jump on you... or else!"ÅToday, we're taking a hiatus from your regularly scheduled roster to visit another relic of Reborn's League History, Kiki Argall!"cNow the modest Sensei of Apophyll Academy, Kiki was once a Fighting Gym Leader of some renown!"yA devout teacher of zen philosophy, Kiki sings the melody that eases the mind and plays the beat to soothe the body."{Her special technique, honed even after her retirement, revolves around honing her Pok√©mon's power with mental focus,"oAnd believe me, a Pok√©mon's power-packed pure Focus Punch isn't something any brawler can just shrug off.")Take special care with her Medicham!"vIts Meditate attack will skyrocket its offensive capabilities, so make sure to take it down before it can set up!"LToday, we're looking at Reborn's newest Leader, the poison-packing Aya!"|A new star on the scene, Aya has recently replaced her own brother, Cain LaRue, who himself was a relatively recent arrival!"dIt seems between the two of them, they decided she's the better fit for the role of Gym Leader!"^My sources tell me that Aya, who lives in the Byxbysion Wasteland, favors Double Battles,"bAnd uses her signature move to throw all the putrid power of poison across the field at once."-Take care, or you really will be wasted!"DOf course, none carries this task out better than her Dragalge."FIts Adaptability skill makes any hit sting, so KO that 'Mon ASAP."6Today we're looking at the Ice Gym Leader, Serra!"iA former model, Miss Serra Voclain has made a career change and is now breaking up the battle scene."wFor Trainers daring to bear Serra's feral onslaught, beware and take care to prepare for this icy hell of a fight!"[Always one for keeping appearances, Serra's arena is covered top to bottom in mirrors."âHer stealthy Pok√©mon, notably Froslass, enjoy dancing in and out of the frames, both silver and glass, with a tinge of aurora for shine!"åDefensive and sneaky plays are the name of her Pok√©mons' game, so reliable attacks or those that can shatter her screens can be your go-to!"`Before going in, reflect on how you can see past her tactics and pin the pin-up model down!"Let's talk about Noel!"sOne of Reborn's youngest Leaders, this prodigy boy has an arena set up right below the Lapis Ward's Orphanage."HNoel's got a penchant for frustrating his unsuspecting challengers,"ZWho suppose either his youth or his Normal-type Pok√©mon will make for an easy match."\Not to be outdone so easily, Noel packs a medley of Pok√©mon that cover his weaknesses."6Including, to the surprise of many, his Clefable!"zThough Clefable is no longer a Normal-type Pok√©mon, Noel is one of the few Leaders to use a wildcard in his battles."óDon't let yourself get stuck on this brick wall of a Pok√©mon, and do whatever it takes to take it out before it gets cozy in its defensive capability!"ÜBy the way, a few of our listeners have asked in the past about just how someone of Noel's age earned a position in the Reborn League."tLike any Leader, he was referred to the position and passed his qualifying tests-- with flying colors, no less!"5But just who would refer him to such a position?"AWe'll give you just a small hint! All right, listen closely:"
"...""HWe've got a report on Grandmaster Radomus, Reborn's Psychic Leader!"BRadomus is a cheery man with a fascination for assorted hats!"Ranging from fashionable to outright bizarre, his wardrobe and mannerisms toe the line between defying and defining logic!"COf course, as a Grandmaster of chess, his logic must be solid."{Having amassed a fortune from tournaments, he lives in his very own personal Castle, complete with a Chessboard Arena!"rIn battle, his Psychic abilities can shift the pieces around, including making them attack your own Pok√©mon."/Fight back by beating him at his own game!"His ace Pok√©mon is already well known herself, the one and only Gossip Gardevoir, who runs other segments on the network."úHer strength is matched only by her pep, so make sure you're ready when going into battle, otherwise you'll find yourself right in check by the two of them!"+Let's talk about the Gym Leader, Luna!"GLuna's a lovely lady with more than one way to make a man tremble."}If her beauty wasn't spell-binding alone, her Dark-type attacks will lock down and take out any opposition if unchecked."äAnd from being the Champion of Wonderland, to a regal lord's maid, Luna enjoys bringing infinity to reality by living out storybook tales."GEven her Pok√©mon are all named after characters from old fantasy!"AAs for what they are, we'll let you figure out the hard way."=After all, the Cheshire Cat himself was never too clear."$One-and-two, that's a knockout!"KYou'll hear this often when facing the Agate Circus Strongman, Samson!"qReborn's current Fighting Gym Leader, compared to the long past previous one, is all about matter over mind!"íHis Pok√©mons' power is augmented by the Big Top's High Striker effect, an infamously rigged carnival game that triggers based on certain attacks!"]Here's a hook: It turns out, Samson may not have joined the League of his own according.";It seems he was strong-armed into it by another party."And who's that?"<None other than the Agate Circus' Ground Leader, Terra!"What could have gone down?"The world may never know."<But in order to take him out, beat him at his own game!"òCripple his Pok√©mon to reduce their power-- even that from the High Striker-- or use the Big Top's Flying-type advantages for the super-effective kill!"ÄEither way, Pok√©mon like his ace, Conkeldurr, are sure not to go down easy as they tank hits and strike back double every time!"MToday, we're going over Charlotte, a young beauty as cool as she is hot!"ÖTaking over her mother's Gym after years of absence, Charlotte's Super-heated Field offers little advantage itself to her Fire-types."~However, when ignited by her wide-ranged Fire attacks, the inferno takes a new life, and often a few other lives with it!"nTrainers will need to keep the flames under wraps one way or another, or pack a team that can stand them!"HThe situation gets no more mild when her Ninetales enters the fray!"pIts Drought Ability amplifies her strength even further, but keep in mind, every strategy has its exploits!"HShe's hearty, she's hyper, and she's abso-freaking- lutely insane--"1Terra, the Ground Gym Leader, is up to play!"oWith a personality like an earthquake and a type to match, anyone who's met her-- is probably traumatized."rHowever, I wanted to find out what's really behind that energetic persona, so I did some digging to find out."{From the records I found, it looks like Terra was a fairly average girl at one point, having been raised in the Beryl Ward."qSchool reports say she was very shy, and seldom socialized, and took a natural interest in computer science."TOne day, however, she ran away from home for a reason perhaps she only knows..."b...and was next known applying for a job at the Agate Circus with her zany energetic persona!"aJust what happened to her between the time she left home and the time she joined the Circus?".Call me crazy-- Actually, call her crazy,")But I'm not sure I want to find out."1Let's talk about the aerial Agate Ace, Ciel!":If you haven't seen her in action, then imagine this:"'Two ribbons hang from the ceiling."îA dancer on the floor twirls herself betwixt them, over, under, and back again, spinning this way and that, pulling the ribbons ever tighter to her."Then--"She jumps."KThe ribbons unfurl around her body, lifting her up with their tension."eShe grabs onto them, subtly climbing higher as she flips over, her legs dancing towards the sky."pShe can walk, swing, float in mid air, all between these ribbons, moving like water through the atmosphere."TThe crowd gazes in silent awe as she moves against gravity and with the melody,"ZGracefully rolling herself into an angel's sleeve, and descending to the Earth again."AIt's undeniable-- nothing can match Ciel's grace and beauty!"@In fact, some day, I'd like to get her in for an interview."*"Ciel, tell us-- What's your number?""LSorry, listeners, but I'm not broadcasting the answer to that question."QToday I'd like to talk about Reborn's Fairy-type Gym Leader, Adrienn Flores."IPersonally speaking, I've only gotten to know Adrienn very recently,"rBut I'd like to think that in our time working together around Reborn City, we've become pretty good friends."rAdrienn's that sort of person who knows how to sing xyr spirit into every syllable, and believe me, it shows."íIn just the small amount of time xe's been around, xe's been able to attract more people to xyr life and xyr cause than anyone else I've ever met."$Hold up, that gives me an idea."UI've got a feeling that Adrienn would give some out-of-this-world dating advice."úListeners, if you'd be interested in having Adrienn on the show for a segment, why don't you hit us up on Chatter and let us know what questions you'd have."~But back to the silver-haired silvertongue's day-to- day dealings, don't mistake xyr softness of heart for softness in battle."ìAdrienn's battle style numbers in Doubles, and a Fairy pairing makes a very scary and fairly harrying team tearing into challengers left and right!"jIn particular, watch out for xyr Florges, Rhyannon-- a Pok√©mon that might as well run in xyr family."âWith mixed moves to pack a pixie punch and more bulk than a beefed-up Blissey, it's gonna take a team effort to uproot this flower power."NBut I gotta be honest with you guys-- I haven't had the best time lately."Had a little accident--"EAnd let's just say it's a miracle I'm fit to go on TV right now."$Eye patches are stylish, right?"LI'll spare you all the details-- some of them are unclear to me anyway."4But for those who might be concerned-- no need."fWhat doesn't kill us makes us stronger, but probably needs to be pummeled into the ground anyway."HEnough about me-- we've got a Gym Leader profile to steal the show."PAnd who better to steal it than the Steel Leader herself, Titania Andersen."]Now Tania, as her friends call her, ain' the most friendly Leader on the chopping block."VShe's got a personality harder than her element and a temper on the cutting edge."UBut this smoldering beauty is forged of more than just a metal mettle and flare."cYou'd never know from looking, but this lass has a literary lineage and the interest to match."õI'm told that above all other subjects in her education at the Onyx Trainers' School-- even battling-- Miss Titania chose to prioritize classic literature."äWho knows what about turning pages turns her head, but maybe it's this archaic aesthetic that draws her to older arts like drawing blades."VFor a girl known to swing around her Aegislash as easily as if it were an √©p√©e,"VIt should be no surprise that the blade and buckle Pok√©mon also acts as her ace!"hThose who intend to take arms against her should take care not to lose their own during the battle!"rToday we'll be talking about an admirable allure in the astounding alacrity of the aqua artist, Amaria Fiore!"ÖAmaria is Reborn's most senior Leader-- not in age, mind you, as this maritime maiden is as fair on the eyes as she is on the heart--"ÜBut despite her youth, she was the first Leader chosen by former Champion and Reborn League Manager Ame to take up a Gym Leader title."{Apparently, the two of them were somehow close friends and inspired each other to take steps to reopen the old League!"{So for all those Trainers out there enjoying Reborn and its challenges, remember-- you've got Amaria Fiore to thank for it!"iThe lass has also made quite a splash in Reborn City's development in the past even aside from that,"~Having been responsible for tracking down and shutting up some of Reborn City's most environmentally-damaging facilities."[Those who've seen her in action know that her star player, a Lapras named Deliverance,"TShould only be underestimated by those who want to themselves be dragged under."BAnd how does a Pok√©mon get a name like that, you may wonder."\From what Miss Amaria has said in the past, it seems like it earned its name firsthand."}She tells a story about a time when she was swimming far out from the coast, only to be caught in the middle of a storm!"eMake no mistake-- Amy is a stunning swimmer, but stormy seas can sink even the most stout ships."êSo it was when Amaria thought she'd drawn her last breath that she found herself pulled first to the surface and second to safety by a Pok√©mon!"oThat Pok√©mon would be her lifelong companion, who she named Deliverance in thanks for it saving her life."ìTurns out, Deliverance saves more than just lives though, with many of Amaria's past challengers having been staring it down as the face of defeat,"8In what otherwise seemed like a won match for them."DAs Amaria announces-- Deliverance always pulls through for her!"xWe've got a special program rolling out for you today on the Rock-type and rockin' roller renegade, Hardy Andersen!"wIf that last name sounds familiar to you, it should-- He's the younger brother of Steel Leader Titania Andersen..."FAnd in a sense, he's got her to thank for his stairway to heaven!"pYou see, nowadays there isn't a whole lotta love between them, but they weren't always in such bad company."tBack in the glory days, the two of them were thick as thieves, united in their interest for Rock-type Pok√©mon!"ãBut when Steel-types were discovered and were all the latest pride and joy of the Pok√©mon world, Titania jumped ship and went her own way!"WShe never looked back, but Hardy was determined to dream on with his classic type!"`And thus started an enduring rivalry between the siblings-- one that don't stop even today!"óHardy's held that determination fast to take care of business and rise up in the ranks, raring to prove once and for all just which is the better type!"kAnd indeed, Hardy isn't just another brick in the cabal of Rock Leaders at the bottom of their totems."sAs the second highest-ranked Leader in Reborn, that boy promises to rock all his challengers like a hurricane!"^Challengers looking to face down Hardy should take extra care for his Dusk Form Lycanroc!"vThis beast of burden promises to send any challenger free-fallin' unless they escape just by the hair of the dog!")And that's more than just a feeling."lOn the chopping block today is the top-brass battler, gold medalist among the masters, Saphira Belrose!"ÉThis Dragon Type dame is a destructive force not to be fought lightly, as she vouchsafes her type's reputation as the kings of old!"HAnd speaking of reputations, it'd seem that one runs in the family."}Saphira inherits her gym and power in two-step from her father, Montague Belrose, of the previous generation of Leaders."âThose who've remained in or returned to the region since old days might remember the fiery competition between he and Caroline Flambairn.">For those a little fresher to scene, so the story goes..."[The two Leaders met after being stationed adjacent to each other between their cities."ÖTrue to her type, little Caroline was as hot-headed as they come, and from the outset she resented any competition from her neighbor!"yAfter a spell of trying to outdo Monty in performance alone, she tried to prove herself by challenging him directly!"UBut chalk it up to a difference in rank, the type chart, or whatever you like..."No dice!".In a total sweep, Caroline hit the floor.".But the blazing broad up and tried again,"And again,"And again..."rMonths went by, and the sight of little Caroline fuming away from Monty's Gym was practically a daily ritual."àAs all good stories must, though, this came to an end when she finally scored a win, proving her hard- earned strength once and for all!"èThe victory was a blessing to the regulars, tired of hearing howls of anger and annoyance each day when the Fire Type femme flew off the scene."ë...So, you can imagine their shock and disappointment when, the next day after winning, Caroline once again showed up on Monty's doorstep anyway!"ÅNo one is quite sure what happened in the gym that day in particular, but rumor has it the two were quite inseparable after that!"hAnd that blustering legacy lives on even now with their children having taken over their positions!"TAs for Saphira, the modern challenger may want to take one note of this legacy."vHer arena was rebuilt in the recent reconstruction of Labradorra City, but one hold-over from her father remains:"DA certain game old Montague is said to have been quite fond of,"EThat he would make all his challengers play before fighting him."dChallengers, come stocked on potions and ready to fight to claim the title of king of the hill!"&The unprepared may yet regret it."GWhen fighting Saphira herself, watch out for her famous Dragonite!"àThis multiscaled menace has hampered more than a few matches in its primetime, using its diamond defense out the door to set up a sweep!"$I'll give you a hint, Trainers!">In her arena, there's only one type it's truly weak to..."2Get in there and get ready to rock its world!"0That's all for now, but remember, Trainers,".Keep fighting with everything you've got!"GHold your spirits high, and even you can defeat the Reborn League!",And now, a public service announcement:"@Crime and pollution are at an all-time high in Reborn City."(But it doesn't have to be that way.";Do your part! Pick up where you can, and never litter!"<Together we can keep Reborn's streets and waters clean."For a better Reborn."Need Potions?"Pok√© Balls?"!Vitamins, Repels, Antidotes?"RBerries, TMs, Awakenings, Battle Items, Freeze Heals, Burn Heals, Full Heals,"3Every kind of heal you could possibly imagine!"oEvolution stones, evolution items, items for luck, items for unluck, items for having too many damn items!"You need it?"We got it."You don't need it?"We got that too.""The Obsidia Department Store,"LLocated in Central Obsidia at 11th and Saffron, sponsored by Silph Co.!"NGoing out soon? Or do you need to drop off your friend for some playtime?"LCome to the Obsidia Day Care on Goldenrod Street, now back in business!":We'll take care of your Pok√©mon just like you would."&The Obsidia Day Care is now open!"Give us your Pok√©mon!"<We will make them stronger than you could ever imagine!"CWe have no cap on the number of Pok√©mon we can raise for you!"ESo be sure and turn them all in to raise yourself a proper army!"<You can be the strongest Trainer if you just come here!"KThe Obsidia Day Care, located in Central Obsidia at Goldenrod and 9th."6How are you doing today? And how's your Pok√©mon?"RIf your day is anything less than perfect, come by the Central Obsidia Salon!"dOur first class services are provided by the top Pok√©mon breeders and caretakers in the world!"nA quick stay here is guaranteed to make you smile, and never fails to bring you and your Pok√©mon closer!"UCheck us out! Central Obsidia Salon, located on Main Street in the Obsidia Ward."'Trainers! Looking for a challenge?"6Think you have what it takes to rise to the top?!"4The Reborn League is now accepting challengers!"]Pit your Pok√©mon against our legion of 18 typed Gym Leaders-- the best in the business."}For the best of the best, 18 Badges earns you the right to challenge the famous Elite Four, and then the mysterious Champion!"Don't be shy!"3Stop by the Grand Hall in the Opal Ward today!"$Check out the Reborn Nightclub~"'Want some wild nights? Hot action?"JWe're talking raves! Dancing, battles, music, this is the night life!"XCheck us out in the North Obsidia Ward, on Castelia Street near the Grand Stairway!"Ride in style!"+Check out the Lapis Luxury Cycle Shop!"8We have better bikes than anyone else in the world!"/For the top, perfection knows no pricetag!"5Check us out in the Lapis Ward at Peony and 4th!"/Looking to become a top Trainer in Reborn?"1The Onyx Trainers' School has what YOU need.".We cater to students of all skill levels."}Headed by one of Reborn's own Gym Leaders, the Onyx Trainers' School promises a learning experience you'll never forget!"RThe Onyx Trainers' School is a franchise of the Pok√©mon Technical Institute."QThe Pok√©mon Technical Institute is pleased to offer its services to Reborn."<Enroll today in the Onyx Ward at 11th and Ivyline Road."-The Reborn Silph Co. Branch is now open."ASilph Co. is one of the oldest corporate names in the world."5Now we're here to offer you our finest services."&Silph Co.-- A name you can trust."Need a treat?"Aching for sweets?"0We've got the thing to beat the other eats!"+The Sweet Kiss Candy Shop is now open!"çWe've got everything from Common Candy to Rare Candy-- and a whole host of delicious non-black licorice candy for both you AND your Pok√©mon!"qWe know you have a sweet tooth, and you should, as our products rival even major medicines in their effects!"RCheck out our upcoming competitions too, for a chance to win a rare Pok√©mon!"WRemember, there's no need to be confused-- Sweet Kiss is your one-stop candy shop.",Come in today, to 10th and Main Street!" Need a break from studying?"From work?"?Want the coolest place to hang out with the hottest games?"6Check out the Onyx Arcade on 11th and Easterling!"TWe've got great games and fabulous prizes for both the hardcore and the casual!"Ready, set... Game on!"SAre you tired of the bleak grey and black grimy get- up of the city spectacle?"Come visit Sweet Scent!"ZReborn's very own flower shop, located in the Lapis Ward at 3rd and Hydrangea Street!"HWe guarantee the perfect floral flourish for any apartment or home."1Check us out, and you won't be disappointed!"YRINGMASTER: Hello, hello, boys, girls, ladies, gentlemen, and everything in between!"]Agate Circus is open for business under a new owner, and boy, do we have a show for you!"õWe have the greatest show in all of Reborn featuring a host of zany clowns, the strongest man you'll ever meet, and the alluring charm of an aerial ballet!"We have games!"Candy!"Pok√©mon!"2Our main show now includes 500% more Donphan!"BNo, seriously, we have so many Donphan here that it's stupid!"@So come on and do something! Anything! At the Agate Circus!"CRITICAL CAPTURE!"çLocated on 9th and Main Street in the Central Obsidia Ward, Critical Capture has a unique variety of Pok√© Balls to suit any Trainer's needs."'Come on by and catch a great deal!"!Helllllo there, Reborn City."(We know that times have been tough."}And in these tough times, sometimes it's hard to find a minute-- or a place-- to sit down, relax, and have a cold drink."-Why don't you come on down to the Spyce?"BFeaturing good eats, smooth music, and the best beer in town,"The Spyce has it all."KFind us on 9th Street by Castelia. Come on in, and Spyce up your life.""Need to spice up your roster?"Looking for new Pok√©mon?"(Welcome to Reborn's Pok√©mon Watch!"\Today, we're looking for Pok√©mon in the Peridot and Opal Wards! What is there to find?"ÅWell, rumour has it that sometimes a cheery blue Pok√©mon can be seen dancing around the fountain in North Peridot when it rains."QToday, we're looking at the small reserve of wildlife around the Grand Hall."3Only a few species can be found here, however."Oh, my, is that a Combee?"#Where could it have come from?"9There certainly aren't any in the grass around here."How curious!".This morning, we visited a secret garden."rThe owner of the garden wishes to keep himself and its location anonymous, but there were some neat Pok√©mon!"fIn fact, we even saw a group of Cherubi! Fascinating how such things live right under our noses.."HUnfortunately, the Cherubi had made themselves scarce by afternoon."(Perhaps they like the morning cool?"RToday, we're looking for Pok√©mon in the South Obsidia, Coral and Onyx Wards!"|Rumour has it that deep in the Obsidia Slums, there's a secret room where a certain species of beefy Pok√©mon hang out!"ÇNormally on this show, we only talk about wild Pok√©mon, but I just saw this energetic Lillipup, and can't help but talk about it!"FThe feisty thing was dragging its poor Trainer all over the city!"#By the West Peridot Factory..."...to under Opal Bridge..."#...back up to North Peridot..."-...or in the back of the Obsidia Ward..."$...even down to the Coral Ward!"-Finally, they ended up in the Onyx Ward!"/There's no telling where that pup will go!"qToday, we were passing through the Coral Ward, down around the warehouses, and there was this awful banging.":It almost sounded like a Pok√©mon was trapped inside."#But I wonder what it could be?"EToday, we're looking for Pok√©mon in the Jasper and Beryl Wards!"ÖActually, earlier today we came across a police officer who was looking for a certain Pok√©mon and had a rare Egg to offer in return!"?I smell an opportunity for one generous and lucky Trainer!"CIn fact, just last night we passed through the Beryl Cemetery."$It was a terrifying experience!"<I was afraid that a zombie would rise up and attack me!"%And to my fright, something did!"zWell, our cameraman turned tail and fled before we could catch the culprit on film, so as of yet, it is unidentified."aBut for all you brave Trainers out there, be warned that there could be something lurking..."&Ah, wait, what's this over here?!"!It's an Aipom! What a cutie!",Oh, hey, no, don't run away! Come back!"-Ah, it scampered back up into that tree."VNo matter, we still know that there are Aipom in this area now! What a rare find!"LToday, we're looking for Pok√©mon in the North Obsidia and Lapis Wards!"ZWe're chasing rumors of a rare Pok√©mon digging around behind the streets of Obsidia!"CThis howling black beast is said to be extremely elusive, but!"7We've been tracking it, and we think we've found--"0???: 'Ey, you trespassin' on our territory?"@HOST: Oh, um, hi, what? No, sir! We're just innocent news--"3???: Get outta here! Or I'll make you get out!"HOST: Okay!"ãFollowing rumors of a rare Pok√©mon having been seen in the area, we've tracked it down to this location: A lavish house in the Lapis Ward.">Let's find out if we can meet the owner of this rare Po--"3CRAUDBURRY: What's all that racket out there?!",HOST: Ah, hello! Are you the owner of--"NCRAUDBURRY: I don't need your scandalous press loitering around my house!"RThis is MY property, and I can have you arrested for filming without consent!"#HOST: Miss, please calm down--"/CRAUDBURRY: What's your network? I'll sue!".Stand right there, I'm getting my lawyer!"JHOST: Yikes, and after everything we couldn't find any Pok√©mon. Bye!"/You will not BELIEVE what we've just seen!"0A legendary Pok√©mon, right here in Reborn!"CBefore our eyes, a beautiful Mew jumped right by and vanished!"FWe're on the hunt now! We know it ran this way, and-- Oh my word!"/That's a Victini! Two legends in one day?!"What is this?!"Quick, follow it!"Aw, where did it go?"Wait, back there! It's a--"Darkrai?!"*Wait, it just transformed into... Oh!"It's a Zorua!"But it ran off..."7Trainers, keep an eye out for this illusive catch!")It could take the shape of anything!"<Today, we're looking for Pok√©mon all over Reborn City!"áFollowing a beaten path off from the Beryl Cemetery, we come through a dark cave to a place somewhere deep in the Rhodochrine Jungle..."6What kind of mysterious Pok√©mon will we-- Aah!!!"=What? We seem to have been trapped in some sort of cage!")What Pok√©mon could have done this?!"*We've got a special report coming in!"mSean Slagle from the Peridot Ward writes to us about a strange Pok√©mon that appears only when it rains!"6You might expect that this would be a Water-type!"3But no! It's actually, of all things, a Numel!"_Sean tells us that the poor Pok√©mon wanders out in every storm looking lost and confused."mIt‚Äôs obviously suffering from the rain, but the strange thing can't figure out what to do with itself!"TToday we were checking out the alleys of the city when we found a certain pool."oTwo surprises awaited us-- the first being that the water in this place was miraculously not contaminated."BThe second being that it was teeming with dangerous Pok√©mon?"Which?"/We'll let our viewers find out themselves!"QToday, we're looking for Pok√©mon around Apophyll Beach and Pyrous Mountain!"5We're exploring a cave far out across the beach."-There's no telling what could be inside!"Hey, what's that!"!Moving there in the shadows!"(What kind of Pok√©mon could it be!?"It's a--"Oh, it's just a Stunfisk."That's not exciting."3Cut, cut. We'll have to look somewhere else..."iJust today we were walking down the beach, when suddenly one of the volcanic stones started shaking!"WAnxious to uncover the source of this tremor, we smashed open the rock in a hurry.""Inside was a unique Pok√©mon!"It's Shuckle!"How strange!"RBut it didn't seem like there would be very many. Could this be a rare find?!"PWe've been tracking a mysterious Pok√©mon in the depths of Pyrous Mountain!"}This lava-loving creature is elusive and lonesome, but after dedicated research, I think we've finally found its habits."And they're quite silly!"ôIt seems this Pok√©mon loves to eat molten stone and other minerals... but with the volatile lava flow in Pyrous Mountain, sometimes falls right into it!"OThus, we wound up finding this Pok√©mon stuck in some other cooling magma!"_It seems this Pok√©mon crawls off to brood on its own in a far off, but very heated place!"6We weren't able to get our attention ourselves...";But a clever Trainer could perhaps lure it to a catch!"YToday, we're looking for Pok√©mon around Azurine Island and the Byxbysion Wasteland!"4However, horror has struck us in the Wasteland!"aAfter being bafflingly lost inside the hallowed halls and walls of the mountainous tundra..."-An apparition has revealed itself to us!"{Needless to say, we high-tailed it out of there, but a braver Trainer may find a prize for themselves if they dare face it!"nThis morning, we were traveling through Azurine Island, and one of our cameramen leaned on a nearby tree."`Imagine his surprise when a spirited Psychic-type fell out of it, right on top of his head!"They were NOT happy!"}Today, we were relaxing in the Wasteland-- if one can 'relax' in such a chaotic place-- when we chanced upon an adorable duo."?Two young Nidoran were playing in the Wasteland's tunnels!"KNot ideal scenery, but the young Pok√©mon were a picture-perfect pair."fToo bad they scampered off, but there seem to be Nidoran out there waiting for a Trainer to find!"BToday, we're searching the Chrysolia Region for new Pok√©mon!"TThis morning, we found a hidden clearing in the middle of the Chrysolia Forest!"ãAlthough we didn't find any Pok√©mon, we did find another little gem that could be useful to Trainers: A rock positively glowing with moss!"$Who might find this useful, hm?"%Could such a Pok√©mon be nearby?"&We've unveiled quite the mystery!"5Late last night, our group stumbled upon a cave."oThe inside of the cave was very confusing, winding in circles, almost like a riddle-- but never mind that!"/Let's talk about the rare Pok√©mon inside!"-By some luck, we encountered a Smeargle!"kWith its Sketch attack, it could be an invaluable tool for any breeder that can get their hands on it."aThis evening, we're searching the shore of a surprisingly pure lake in the Chrysolia Region!"^With all the pollution around the city, it's a marvel that a place like this could exist!"REven more marvelous, tons of Pok√©mon flock to its shore, and many cute ones!"^But one cutie especially caught our eye: A little Poliwag wagging its way along the lake!"HMaybe some Trainer might like to add this doll to their collection!"BToday, we're looking in the vast Aventurine Region of Reborn!"(Oh! Look at that! It's a Heracross!"%And not only that, but a Pinsir!"%The two are fighting each other!"2Perhaps they're after the honey on that tree!"[Yet, they're locked in a fierce combat. These two Pok√©mon are ignoring us completely!"ÄI would be surprised if there were any way a Trainer could get their attention long enough to even smack them with a Pok√© Ball!"BBut maybe there's some way to get them alone to capture them?"FWe've traveled deep into the woods and we've found a hidden cave."/What wonders might this cave hold for us!?"UOh, my! Ice crystals jet up from the floor to-and-fro, and in the middle-- look!"#Icy mist rolls off that stone!"-Could it be emitting some special power?">I can think of at least one species who would enjoy that!"rWe've been taking a peaceful stroll through the woods, following a lovely tune performed for us this evening."[What sort of Pok√©mon could be such a divine singer? It must be so cute, and innocent!"âWe'll leave that question for you to answer, Trainers, because this is a Pok√©mon that doesn't appear to us walking around on the ground!"4Perhaps the answer is in the trees, or the sky!"MToday, we're searching for Pok√©mon around the Agate Circus and Route 2!"bWe're out on an early morning adventure to see what we can see on the peaks outside of Agate."6Oh! Look at that! It's a whole flock of Hawlucha!"qThese bizarre Pok√©mon seem to gravitate to this area in the mornings for their workout habits. Now we know!"?We're here at the Agate Circus and we were VERY surprised."VWe weren't promised a Pok√©mon as a prize, but it seems one snuck into the booth!"*Much to the game operator's surprise!"IWell, he wanted to get rid of it, so we're now the proud new owners." Maybe you can luck out too!"\So, here's a shout-out to and signal boost for a rather enigmatic man whom we just met."Somewhere near the Circus, this man offers a deal-- find which Pok√©mon to trade him in return for his rather rare Vulpix!"9Any interested Trainers should seek him out at once!"MToday, we're looking for Pok√©mon in the greater Ametrine Mountain area!"iWe're traveling through Celestinine Mountain right now, and we've got a rare Pok√©mon in our sights!"dIt appears to be training its strength using some of the boulders as punching bags! Impressive!"CPerhaps it might come to respect one who can prove its better?"tWe've been diving deep beneath Ametrine Mountain in search of rare Water Pok√©mon, and boy have we found one..."ZSplashing about in crested pools deep below Ametrine Mountain-- would you believe it?"It's a Totodile!"äGood luck catching the spirited little thing though, it weaves in and out of the water as easily as Ciel Featherstone swings in the skies!"ìToday we're taking an underwater exploration, where we received an anonymous tip that a certain Pok√©mon appears only on a certain day of the week!"G...Unfortunately, we've had no luck finding the rare Lapras yet..."CIs it because this hollow underground area is so big and vast?")Or did we just get the day wrong...?"CI could've sworn there was some historical precedent for it..."qWell, we can't keep the equipment submerged for too long, so it looks like we'll be signing out of this one!"NToday, we're looking for Pok√©mon around the Ametrine Mountain peak area!"2Instead, we've heard a very concerning story!"wAmetrine is famous for its snow-capped peaks and frigid temperatures, and few Pok√©mon are able to withstand it..."\But according to one report, a foreign Pok√©mon has been abandoned among the icy peaks!" Will this Pok√©mon be okay?"ÄTrainers in the area, keep a lookout for any defenseless Pok√©mon that may have been abandoned, and make sure to keep them safe!"uWe were passing by a large building in Ametrine City this evening and were surprised to discover something rare!"IAn Old Amber was just laying half-buried in the snow in front of us!"\Unfortunately, a child came and claimed the item as 'his treasure' that he had dropped."6But could there be more Old Amber somewhere here?"YAs you might know, Ametrine City is somewhat renowned for its technological prowess."FOne of the few industries that can be maintained in such climate."ROccasionally, in sorting through the computers, you find some strange things!"YToday we've found a machine that can actually alter the form of a specific Pok√©mon!"]It requires a Data Chip to work, but if you have one, you can freely use it at any time!"qToday, we're back in Reborn City, peeping the Pok√©mon that are once again popping up all around the region!"ëAnd let me tell you, Trainers, I've already had my Sawks Knocked Off by the sheer volume and strength that resurfacing wildlife has been showing."kJust the other night, we were traveling in the Jasper Ward and we came across-- you won't believe it--"zA huge, fully evolved Ampharos, nightlight tail-wagging like a pendulum as it lumbered around the quiet city streets."cSeeing something so peaceful return to this city after so long was a truly sublime experience."yNot only that, but reports of such powerful Pok√©mon peacefully returning to the area have been pouring in recently."YOnce upon a time, it was thought that the wildlife had fled the tainted Reborn City."EIt turns out, it was just waiting until the day it could return."sHere on Reborn's Pok√©mon Watch, we've been dipping our toes and our lures into a newly purified Azurine Lake."YReborn's Water Treatment Center seems to have bounced back with an unexpected vigor,"UWorking overtime to clear out every bit of muck from the once-sullied waterland."4Meanwhile, the Pok√©mon have responded in kind."lHow they survived the toxic onslaught of pollution past may remain a mystery to us humans for all time,"gBut there's no denying the numerous species fishers are rejoicing to see in their lake once again."GJust this morning, one of our crewmen fished up a whole Eelektrik!"vWe would've loved to show you the footage, but unfortunately the Pok√©mon's Electric attack fried our video feed."aStill, there's definitely more out there in the depths than we could have possibly expected."JWe've been chasing a rare specimen through the sewers under the city!"äWhen exploring the recently reactivated Water Treatment Center for any signs of life, we came across none other than the ultra-rare Goomy!"{Of course, when pursuing it, the Pok√©mon hopped into one of the pipes and slid its way out of grasp into a back room."^Perhaps some other Trainer will be able to plunge this purple Pok√©mon from the pipeline,"+But we here are hunters, not plumbers."$And it still smells down there."	Bad."VWe're out in full force in the Tourmaline Desert and its surrounding areas today!"EThe desert itself is, as many would expect, considerably empty--"fBut for Trainers willing to venture off the beaten path, who knows what may be in store for them?"iWe've been searching for a while now and have come to a very strange place indeed where the sky is--"What?!"Are you okay!?"Hey! Hey, answer me!"One second--"/Sorry, viewers, for the distorted footage!"kAs our cameraman was filming, something just fell out of the tree above him and knocked him clean out!"Hold on, let me--"4Gosh, how does he carry this thing everywhere--"There! You can see it!"It's a Ferroseed!"UWho knew that a Pok√©mon like that would be hiding in a tree here of all places!"NOkay, anyway, our crewman needs medical attention, so we'll be going now!"FFor instance, we may have just made the discovery of our careers!"`We're here among the sands right now, and we've discovered, in our very own Reborn Region--"Real--"
Live!"Legendary Pok√©mon!".In fact, this place is teeming with them!",Yet, say, how did we get here anyway..."VWe passed this very spot several times before and there was nothing here before--"HBut now the water is clear and this little thing is just adorable--":Say, if we couldn't see it before, maybe it chose us?"@In that case, perhaps it's disrespectful to broadcast it..."[Mmm... Sorry, Trainers, it seems this isn't a place you'll be able to get to normally!"Even so--"sIn fact, just last night we were camping up on Teknite Ridge, a span of mountains that towers over Tourmaline!"%What we saw was beyond stunning!"cI was woken up by my partner as he was filming the most marvelous meteor shower I'd ever seen!"zWe watched from the safety of a cave as sparkling stars dotting the skies fell and crashed into the peaks around us--"dBut imagine our surprise when we found that those lights weren't meteors at all-- but Pok√©mon!"HThat's right, it's Minior, come down from the heavens to say hello!"_Judging by the craters all over the ground, this may be a common location for them anyway!"3And yet, by morning they had all gone already."mStill, now you know-- Teknite Ridge is a place worth visiting at night if you want a Pok√©mon like this!"cToday we're exploring the northeast area of the Carnelia Region around Route 4 and Agate City!"IWhat kind of Pok√©mon might live up here? Let's see what we can see!"QAnd sure enough, there's certainly something worth seeing up here already..."It's a Scyther!"{This much sought-after Pok√©mon appears to appear only rarely up here, but rest assured, the beauty is alive and well!"kThat Scyther in particular has flown the coop, but it appears to be taking off for greener pastures..."8Perhaps they prefer a warmer environment after all?"|We were traversing down the route here... And don't you know, all of these cliffs and waterfalls make for a bumpy adventure!"cUnfortunately we had a little accident, and half of our equipment ended up washing 