Restoration Project yet?"@Much has been done, true, but yet there's still much to do!"XAsking people all around the city how you can help may yield some fruitful results!"'Ey. You got a problem?"`Maaan, the squad and I used to hang out here all the time when we were playin' the streets."EBut they all got on this "city betterment" bullshit and ditched."Fuck that shit, bruh.".Imma kick it right here my own damn self."zHello there! I'm here to answer any questions you might have about the future of the Reborn City Restoration Project!"5We've come a long way in a short period of time."OFor this, we are endlessly thankful for the help of all of our volunteers!"ZThat said, there's still much to do! Would you like to hear about our upcoming plans?"LHere's some of the things we'll be looking at doing in the near future!"DWe have several potential short-term projects awaiting funding."{First, we have some final renovations to finish up on Beryl Wall. Then, we can finally prepare to reopen Grandview Station!"PAfter that, we have several potential short-term projects awaiting funding."HWe'd like to focus on rebuilding the slums area from the ground up."ãOur plan is to convert this area into a low-income housing district and resource center with community gardening and job-finding resources."sSecond, we'll look at reinforcing underground structures and rebuilding an efficient inter-city subway system."ÑFinally, we'll be restarting the Reborn Pok√©mon Reintroduction Project with a brand-new fully furnished facility on Azurine Island."aIf you wish to donate to the city restoration, please talk to the construction manager here."6We are ecstatic to receive any amount of support."IThank you very much for generously supporting us through everything!"*Of course, there's always more to do!"wWe're now beginning a long-term project to purify the Byxbysion Wasteland, and restart efforts to expand the city."RWe hope to be developing the new Byxbysion Ward within the next couple years!