y $500?!"bSALESMAN: Looking for more Pok√©mon? Of course you are! Well, then have I got a deal for you!"IHow would you like to be the proud new owner of one fantastic beast?"fThis Pok√©mon is so powerful, so utterly BAD-ASS, it's been heralded among dragons for centuries!"QFor you, I'll make a special discount, bringing the price down to only $500!"\GWhat do you say?!"Aha! Thank you! Thank you!"!GOON: Heh. Bad-ass, you say?"3Not a bad deal. I think I'll just help myself."The Pok√©mon was stolen!"GOON: See ya, nerds!"@SALESMAN: ...Well, I got my money. That's your problem now!"JERK: See ya, nerds!"mSALESMAN: Buuuut, if you really wanted to get that ultra-rare Pok√©mon, you could try and find that guy."UThugs like him hang out at the end of the tracks in the Peridot Ward. Good luck!"\Hm? You don't have the money, my friend! Come back when you've got it! I'll be waiting!""Hey, you're missing out here!"9We sometimes have some battle enthusiasts over here."RDifferent one every day of the week, and we get an extra turnout on weekends.",You can battle 'em as much as you want."<But we ask them to clear out when new Trainers come by."ñWe don't want some over-zealous 10 year old rocking up with their level 5 starter, nothing else, and proceeding to conk out on the first guy they see."LThe free battle trainers will be back in a bit though; don't you worry."Z...What, did you forget what I said about the free battle trainers being cleared out?"IOr are you talking to me because you want me to bring them in early?"1I mean... I can do that, if you really want."STheir teams are only a little bit above level 10 or so, so it's not too bad...")Should I tell them they can come in?"#...Well, okay. If you're sure."NBut don't blame us if you charge in there without being ready, all right?"All right. You hang tight."#That's probably a fair choice."\Just wait a little bit. They'll show up around the time you're hitting over that level."Oh."FYou must be wondering what happened to the 