.".Imma kick it right here my own damn self."zHello there! I'm here to answer any questions you might have about the future of the Reborn City Restoration Project!"5We've come a long way in a short period of time."OFor this, we are endlessly thankful for the help of all of our volunteers!"ZThat said, there's still much to do! Would you like to hear about our upcoming plans?"LHere's some of the things we'll be looking at doing in the near future!"DWe have several potential short-term projects awaiting funding."{First, we have some final renovations to finish up on Beryl Wall. Then, we can finally prepare to reopen Grandview Station!"PAfter that, we have several potential short-term projects awaiting funding."HWe'd like to focus on rebuilding the slums area from the ground up."ãOur plan is to convert this area into a low-income housing district and resource center with community gardening and job-finding resources."sSecond, we'll look at reinforcing underground structures and rebuilding an efficient inter-city subway system."ÑFinally, we'll be restarting the Reborn Pok√©mon Reintroduction Project with a brand-new fully furnished facility on Azurine Island."aIf you wish to donate to the city restoration, please talk to the construction manager here."6We are ecstatic to receive any amount of support."IThank you very much for generously supporting us through everything!"*Of course, there's always more to do!"wWe're now beginning a long-term project to purify the Byxbysion Wasteland, and restart efforts to expand the city."RWe hope to be developing the new Byxbysion Ward within the next couple years!"SAround this time we also hope to reestablish rail access with the Orre Region."<All of this could not be possible without your support.".From myself and all of Reborn, thank you."=You wanna know something, buddy? I'll tell you a secret."_The lake water's too toxic to fish in, but my buddy's got this swimmin' pool in his house."yWhen the Pok√©mon in Azurine Lake started gettin' sick, he rescued a few of them and kept them in his swimming pool."3Now the place is practically like an aquarium!"BI heard there's a whole secret area under the Grand Stairway."But how could that be?"rMy buddy used to keep a private aquarium. He was super guarded about it, only letting certain people through."`But now that the water's clean again, he released all of those Pok√©mon back into the lake!"gWhat's more, I managed to convince him to turn his tank into a public pool! How sweet is that, eh?"=Isn't it hard to keep track of stat stages all the time?"WBut you can press Control in battle to toggle a view of everyone's current stages!"Nifty, huh?"5There's an old Abandoned Power Plant up north...">I hear kids disappear when it's windy, and show up there."Weird, right?"2So many strange things have been happening..."Howdy, Trainer."%You ain't come at the best time."9Once upon a time, Reborn was an oasis in the desert."ABut then, alla this city sprung up, and the waste from it...")And then what ya see is what ya got."4You take care travelin' around here, all right?"lRumor has it that there was once an old region on the edge of Reborn, but now it's fallen into decay..."'Boy howdy, I'll tell you what for."uI said once this place was an oasis in a desert, and I'm mighty glad that it's startin' to feel like that again."RI came here because I heard there was a League, but it's so poorly organized."uI've been trying to contact a certain Gym Leader for weeks, but his caretaker won't let him battle apparently..."`\GSALESMAN: You're back! So, are you ready to claim this fantastic Pok√©mon for only $500?!"bSALESMAN: Looking for more Pok√©mon? Of course you are! Well, then have I got a deal for you!"IHow would you like to be the proud new owner of one fantastic beast?"fThis Pok√©mon is so powerful, so utterly BAD-ASS, it's been heralded among dragons for centuries!"QFor you, I'll make a special discount, bringing the price down to only $500!"\GWhat do you say?!"Aha! Thank you! Thank you!"!GOON: Heh. Bad-ass, you say?"3Not a bad deal. I think I'll just help myself."The Pok√©mon was stolen!"GOON: See ya, nerds!"@SALESMAN: ...Well, I got my money. That's your problem now!"JERK: See ya, nerds!"mSALESMAN: Buuuut, if you really wanted to get that ultra-rare Pok√©mon, you could try and find that guy."UThugs like him hang out at the end of the tracks in the Peridot Ward. Good luck!"\Hm? You don't have the money, my friend! Come back when you've got it! I'll be waiting!""Hey, you're missing out here!"9We sometimes have some battle enthusiasts over here."RDifferent one every day of the week, and we get an extra turnout on weekends.",You can battle 'em as much as you want."<But we ask them to clear out when new Trainers come by."ñWe don't want some over-zealous 10 year old rocking up with their level 5 starter, nothing else, and proceeding to conk out on the first guy they see."LThe free battle trainers will be back in a bit though; don't you worry."Z...What, did you forget what I said about the free battle trainers being cleared out?"IOr are you talking to me because you want me to bring them in early?"1I mean... I can do that, if you really want."STheir teams are only a little bit above level 10 or so, so it's not too bad...")Should I tell them they can come in?"#...Well, okay. If you're sure."NBut don't blame us if you charge in there without being ready, all right?"All right. You hang tight."#That's probably a fair choice."\Just wait a little bit. They'll show up around the time you're hitting over that level."Oh."FYou must be wondering what happened to the rebattleable Trainers."That's fair."-They all perished in the version update."Terrible incident, really."JIt's okay though, let me just use some necromancy to bring them back."Good bye.")Oh? You seem to be doing quite well!">But are you really satisfied with just your current team?"AMany Trainers raise multiple Pok√©mon-- more than six even--"AAnd swap them out in rotation for their upcoming challenges.".Never consider your doors closed, friend."^We're still finishing up some loose ends on the Beryl Wall repair project, so hang tight!"?Donations and reconstruction will be available again soon."YWe value your interest in helping Reborn City, so we hope you'll check back shortly!"QHello! I accept donations for restoration projects on behalf of Reborn City.";Would you like to donate to one of our projects today?"why are you here lol":That's okay. I hope you'll consider it in the future!"Y\GFor the South Obsidia redevelopment, the remaining repair costs come to $ \v[334]."How much will you donate?"That covers the project!"ZI'll let everyone know that it's been fully funded, and we'll set to work right away."Look forward to it!"QThank you so much. Reborn City will be a better place for your contribution!"Um."_While I admire your zeal to help the city, you don't seem to have that much money on hand."T\GFor the Railnet reconstruction, the remaining repair costs come to $ \v[335]."7That's okay. I hope you consider it in the future!"`\GFor the Azurine Island Nature Center, the remaining construction costs come to $ \v[336]."By the way, since you are the sole proprietary founder for at least one project, we'd like to extend to you our warmest thanks!"qPer policy, we invite you to meet the employees who work so hard with your money to keep this city thriving!"ÅOur employee area is in the basement below here, and as a premier modern founder, you will now be permitted access at will to it."HAll we ask is that you be courteous to the employees working there."<Thank you again for always looking out for Reborn City!"UWe're still finishing up some loose ends on our previous project, so hang tight!"DThank you for your continued generous donations to Reborn City!"DOur next project, the Byxbysion Ward, will take much more time."âAs it is still in the planning phase while we try to clear away the muck, it will probably be some time before we are ready to tackle it."ÅWhile I would not advise expecting it any time soon, I hope you can look forward to a bigger, brighter Reborn City in the future!"OOf course, I recognize that you've been invaluable in helping us out here."<As an extra 'thank you', why don't you take this stone?"%This was left behind after Ame--"<Uh, well, I think she would have wanted you to have it."So, please."HLet's look forward to a bigger, brighter Reborn City in the future.";Why doesn't anywhere sell Great Balls?! It's not fair!"XI mean, the Obsidia Department Store does, but you need a lot of Stickers for that!"PMaybe I should just learn to use the specialty balls from Critical Capture."gShit, man. This stupid City Restoration Project went an' blasted the place I was using as shelter."AHow the fuck they gonna do that? Who the fuck they helpin'?!"|They think just cuz the damn roof's caving in and the walls got holes in 'em that that place ain't important to people?"JThey think we can afford their refurbished high-class estate housing?"Hell fuckin' nawh I can't!"kThey open up some full-on cheap-housing sector in Peridot, sayin' it's better quality than what I got."DI ain't about that bullshit! I want what I got! I want it back!"MSo Imma camp out here 'til I get my old lot back. We rebel in this shit."BVenturing outside the city is actually a nice change of pace."hI've heard Silph Co. is working on a way to make Pok√©mon that evolve by trade use a Stone instead."!Technology is truly amazing!"eThe city has had to spend an unprecedented amount of money in order to patch everything back up."lTrue, the vast majority of the work was done by volunteers who, thanks to Adrienn, showed up in droves."@But resources cost money, and we are well into debt by now."]Although I think we could have been a bit more frugal in our spending, I have no qualms."ÑOne of the best ways Reborn can make money is by investing in our tourist industry. In order to do that, our city must be beautiful."%And soon, it certainly shall be."1Hey there! You wanna check out... The TMNS?!"4You can't hide in your shell forever, you know!"What? You wanna go?"Didn't think so."/You don't know who I am. Care to find out?"#That's okay. No one here does."6I'm going to play a little song. Can you keep up?"Very well..."CHey, c'mere for a sec! Can I ask you something really quickly?"5Ooh, yay! Another person who wants to fight us~?"Let's go, dear!"Awwwwwwh."/Care for a battle? Talk to the lady if so."Come at me, bro."
