er."#I see more than you ever will."But I'll humor you."YI'll ask you three questions. If you can answer all of them, I'll give you a reward."Wanna try it?"9DANIELLE: Question number one-- this is an easy one."IHow many headbutt trees are there in the area around the Grand Hall?"5DANIELLE: That's right. Simple enough, isn't it?":Okay, question two. This one will be a little harder."vAssuming you can see them all from one angle or another, how many satellite dishes are there in the Obsidia Ward?"DANIELLE: Hmph."+Yes, that's right. But that's obvious."bFine. Since you've done well this far, oh mighty questionee, I'll give you a really good one!"Ready?"CHow many banners and ribbons are there inside the Peridot Gym?"DANIELLE: Tch."Fine. That's correct."_I'm so impressed and overcome with wonder at how you could have possibly known the answer."Wowie."VBut I'll keep my promise and give you the reward, if that's really what you want."...Impressive."-Most normal people don't get that right."8You already knew these answers somehow, didn't you?"Well, whatever."0I'll keep my promise and give you a reward."+\PN obtained Field Effect Read-Out 03!")Info on Misty Terrain now available!"DANIELLE: But hey?"TI've been all over Reborn, and I effortlessly pick up this kind of information."|You seem like you've gotten around a fair bit, but I bet I know things about lots of other places you'd never even think of!".So if you wanna try this again, I'm game."QCome back after you've traveled as much as I have, and we'll try this again!"DANIELLE: There!"GJust because you're normal, it doesn't mean you know more than me!"DANIELLE: Wrong!"NSurely you couldn't miss something as big as a satellite dish, could you?"Or are you the blind one?"DANIELLE: Hmm~ Wrong!"?What's the matter? Didn't you pass by there once or twice?"6Did the trees hide from your perfect eyes' sight?"How disappointing.""DANIELLE: Awh. That's no fun."hIf a girl can't even pick on people who assume they're better than her, what's she got to live for?"[DANIELLE: Come back after you've traveled as much as I have, and we'll try this again!"DANIELLE: Yawn."'Did you find all your answers yet?"4DANIELLE: Are we really going to do this again?"ãDoes it bring you a sense of fulfillment knowing you just go specifically looking for the answers instead of learning to observe as you go?"jThere's no point if you do that, but if it really means that much to you, I'll gratify you once more."Don't say I'm not nice."'Are you ready, oh master surveyor?" DANIELLE: Oh, back so soon?"%Did you actually learn anything?"$DANIELLE: We'll see about that."QGrand rematch of the century, battle of the ages and all that: Question one!"IHow many individual train cars are there in the Byxbysion Wasteland?"<DANIELLE: Yeah, yeah, okay. So you can count, big deal."rFor the record, the only reason I'm even doing these 'how many' questions still is for the sake of tradition."*And I wouldn't want to overwhelm you."AQuestion two: How many buildings total are in Ametrine City?"=DANIELLE: Glad that those didn't escape your keen sight."Question three!"MThere's a man who lives in the Aventurine Woods with a bunch of Pikachu."3How many Pikachu are usually inside his house?"lDANIELLE: I'll give you points for that one; it's harder to keep track when they're all running around."But this isn't over yet!"?How many satellite dishes are there in all of Spinel Town?"DANIELLE: That's right!" Trick question! You got me."&Okay, okay. A real one this time!"?How many bookshelves are there in all of Apophyll Academy?",DANIELLE: All right! You're doing well!"IToo well, in fact, so I'm going to throw everything I've got at you!"1Final question! This is for all the cookies!":How many trees are there in all of Chrysolia Forest?!"DANIELLE: ..."......"........."Just kidding!" Even I don't know that one."But I'll let you have it."~Even if you did just go specifically look for the answers, think about what I said about learning to observe and not just see."You're pretty good."Too good, really."2Did you already know what I was going to ask?"1Regardless, that ended up being kind of fun.">So in return for letting me tease you, you can have this."+\PN obtained Field Effect Read-Out 31!",Info on Fairy Tale Field now available!"4DANIELLE: I'd like to travel the world someday."|People always talk about seeing it, but they never mention how each place has different sounds, scents and atmospheres."That's what I live on."rWhen that happens, and I finally go visit everywhere, I'll be sure to get more questions to pick on you with!"DANIELLE: Realllllly?"+Are you really really realllllly sure?"$I think you should check again!"?After all, that seems to be the only way you'll do things."!DANIELLE: Pi-pi, pikachuuuu!"IBy the way, that's Pikachu-eese for "You're wrong and also a loser.""DANIELLE: Ahaha..."No."kYou really didn't learn anything, did you? You can't even remember buildings? Did you not notice them?"$DANIELLE: Out on the first try!"RCome on, it's not like those trains are going anywhere. How do you miss them?"II can practically see them all just by walking around in that place.":DANIELLE: At least you're honest. I can respect that."I'll be waiting!"kDANIELLE: When I can finally travel the world, I'll be sure to get more questions to pick on you with!"DANIELLE: Pardon me?"Oh, pardon me?")You're asking if I can read braille?"Just because I'm blind?"8Don't you think that's stereotyping a bit too much?"ADo you think all blind people are just born knowing braille?"7Do you think something like that is easy to learn?"fJust pick up a book and translate a few sentences to solve a puzzle in a video game or something?"Well, you're right."EIt is easy, and of course I know braille-- I'm not a troglodyte."2Tell me what you need, and be frank about it."..."Mm."1Braille tablets in a newly formed dimension?"8This sounds like a reasonable and believable story."íAnd what makes you think that this