 I see you've made it to the Gym."àThis telecom system connects right to the Grand Hall, so no matter where you are, whenever you get to a Gym, you can call in for advice!"Anyway..."!Wait, you're at Corey's Gym?"'...He's not even a Leader anymore."What are you doing?"~Well, I probably still have some notes around here from before, in case you are going to challenge him for some reason..."BCorey sometimes uses something called a Corrosive Mist Field."UThis scary tactic will poison any active Pok√©mon that it can every single turn!"AAlthough that may sound daunting, it has a glaring weakness."KSince the poison is tied to the mist, you can use the air against him!"TThe noxious gas is combustible, so Fire-type Pok√©mon can eat right through it."-Careful not to use too much fire though!"uOr, if you bring a Pok√©mon that can clear the air, all that's left to do is power through his team like normal."AAs long as you get some breathing room, you'll be just fine!"xCorey's Corrosive Field can be very damaging to some Pok√©mon, particularly anything vulnerable to the Poison-type."ÜOn top of that, it boosts the effects of almost everything to do with poison, and activates attacks like Venoshock and Venom Drench...":But! That means he's got too many eggs in one basket!"VIf you've got Poison, or even Steel-types yourself, his options are very limited!"eSave your offensive Pok√©mon to pick off things that can break through your anti-Poison defense."9Then all you need to do is set up and take him down!"-Good luck with... whatever you're doing."7No one seems to be picking up at the Grand Hall..."9CHIEF: The situation has taken a turn for the worse!"0We followed Corey in here, but he vanished!"[Then those glowing reactors spewed out some kind of gas and my men completely lost it."0They're as you see now-- lost and confused."!What can we do against this?"<If you intend to do something, then this may be of use."+\PN obtained Field Effect Read-Out 11!"0Info on Corrosive Mist Field now available!"ñCHIEF: We have reason to believe that in addition to mind-altering substances, the reactors in this building are capable of creating this environment."Please tread carefully."CHIEF: You defeated Corey?"0That's great, but now we have to catch him.">You go ahead. The police unit will follow behind as able."Obey..."Aagh! ...Huh?"MWhat happened? We came in to arrest Corey, but then... I don't remember."Attack..."Urgh... What happened?"5All I remember is a hissing noise... Gas, maybe?"We are to serve..."WOAH, what's going on?!"IHuh? These vials spit out some kind of poison! What did it do to us?[3"AME: \PN?"3Hey there! So I see you've made it to the Gym."àThis telecom system connects right to the Grand Hall, so no matter where you are, whenever you get to a Gym, you can call in for advice!"Anyway..."!Wait, you're at Corey's Gym?"'...He's not even a Leader anymore."What are you doing?"~Well, I probably still have some notes around here from before, in case you are going to challenge him for some reason..."BCorey sometimes uses something called a Corrosive Mist Field."UThis scary tactic will poison any active Pok√©mon that it can every single turn!"AAlthough that may sound daunting, it has a glaring weakness."KSince the poison is tied to the mist, you can use the air against him!"TThe noxious gas is combustible, so Fire-type Pok√©mon can eat right through it."-Careful not to use too much fire though!"uOr, if you bring a Pok√©mon that can clear the air, all that's left to do is power through his team like normal."AAs long as you get some breathing room, you'll be just fine!"xCorey's Corrosive Field can be very damaging to some Pok√©mon, particularly anything vulnerable to the Poison-type."ÜOn top of that, it boosts the effects of almost everything to do with poison, and activates attacks like Venoshock and Venom Drench...":But! That means he's got too many eggs in one basket!"VIf you've got Poison, or even Steel-types yourself, his options are v