Read?"4The pages have all been marked over or torn up."%"---phie Villeneuvelle Myt-----""The pages are all blank.""Laura Belrose""AGE AT INTAKE: 8 years"AGE AT DISCHARGE: 18 years"-DIAGNOSIS: Obsessive Compulsive Disorder"rNOTES: Client portrays a discomfort with odd numbers, and a particular mild fixation with multiples of eight."wClient describes an elevated level of cognitive discomfort in response to perceived stimuli of germs and bacteria."YClient refuses to perform daily tasks and engage with others without wearing gloves."PClient tends to occupy communal hygiene spaces for several hours at a time."∑Client describes a particular memory in which she was able to maintain emotional composure when fleeing a burning residence by focusing negatively on the feeling of smoke on her skin."éIt is the opinion of this writer that her fixation on cleanliness is an attempt to physically relieve mental discomfort caused by past trauma."éTREATMENT PLAN: Psychoanalytic talk therapy in consideration of how repressed guilt from childhood trauma may contribute to atypical behavior."ECT has been explored as a subsidiary treatment in acute peaks of anxiety, and to correct pervasive emotional imbalances."""Saphira Belrose""AGE AT INTAKE: 15 years".DIAGNOSIS: Oppositional Defiance Disorder"[NOTES: Client displays an alternatively withdrawn and aggressive affect since arrival."[Client portrays a level of possessiveness over her siblings that borders on obsession."~Client villainizes figures of authority in nearly all cases, and may react aggressively and violently when confronted by such."~Client has been responsible for several physical altercations, especially when first adjusting to the living environment."èClient appears to have some disturbances in her memory, describing inconsistent or impossible events, particularly with regards to this writer."üClient appears to harbor an increasingly unrealistic and violent perception of this writer, even going as far as inventing false circumstances and accusations."qThe client appears to compensate for the loss of her parents by acting as the overprotective parent herself."ÄIn taking on the role of the mother figure, she appears to have created a dissonance regarding the missing male parental figure."éThis dissonance and unacknowledged envy has resulted in inappropriate and imagined fantasies and allegations involving male authority figures."íTREATMENT PLAN: Psychoanalytic talk therapy in exploration of how the loss of her parents has affected her relationship with figures of authority."rECT has been frequently necessitated for emotional regulation in response to delusions and violent outbursts."XOTHER NOTES: Former client has applied repeatedly for guardianship of her siblings."êIt is the opinion of this writer that such guardianship would ultimately be detrimental to the mental health and stability of these individuals."ÉDue to her tenuous relationship with both authority and reality, Saphira Belrose is unable to provide an adequate home environment."¢Furthermore, living in close proximity to one still coping with repressed traumas in such unhealthy ways would likely only exacerbate the siblings' own conflicts."ÅAll prior requests for guardianship have been denied, and it is hereby formalized that future requests are not to be considered."""Charlotte Belrose""AGE AT INTAKE: 6 years"/DIAGNOSIS: Antisocial Personality Disorder"GNOTES: Client struggles to identify and process personal emotions."AClient demonstrates a lack of empathy for other individuals."wClient appears to fixate on dynamics of control, often for the purpose of manipulating others to her own impulses."qClient is prone to periodically create power struggles as a method of validation of her own personal agency."ÆClient engages in duplicitous behavior seemingly for the sake of doing so, including smuggling contraband into the facility and lying about otherwise inconsequential matters."ÅClient believes herself to be personally responsible for the death of her parents, and has thoroughly internalized this as guilt."ñHer apathetic emotional affect regarding the incident, and her subsequent emotional detachment appear to be coping mechanisms to withstand the trauma."ÄTREATMENT PLAN: Psychoanalytic talk therapy in exploration of repressed emotions, feelings, and her resistance to vulnerability."]ECT has been explored as a tool to reconnect with and process otherwise-unfelt emotions.""Heather _____"")The form hasn't been filled out yet.""Anna Doe""2DIAGNOSIS: Auditory and Visual Hallucinations"+NOTES: Provided by an anonymous party."=Client demonstrates a worsening disconnect from reality."xClient reports visual hallucinations, such as seeing non-existent burns, scrapes, and moisture around other people."ZClient reports hearing voices coming from imaginary friends or other unknown sources."gAs client matures, client appears to believe in these 'friends' more concretely, rather than less.".Symptoms first began around the age of 9."åClient does not yet meet other conditions for early diagnosis schizophrenia, but the situation will continue to be monitored as it develops."cIt is possible these hallucinations are a disingenuine, attention-seeking pattern of behavior."|This could serve to allow her to create an elevated sense of significance in lack of other legitimate emotional connections."jStaff are advised to ignore all claims of nonexistent stimuli so as to not enable deceptive behavior."ÖTREATMENT PLAN: Psychoanalytic talk therapy for the purpose of directly acknowledging repressed feelings of loneliness and isolation."UECT has been used to experiment with its affects on the reported hallucinations."èOn several occasions, the client reported no longer hearing the described stimulus after sessions, however, this success has been inconsistent.""Noel Doe""(DIAGNOSIS: Autism Spectrum Disorder"|Client is able to verbally communicate about feelings and experiences, but does not express emotional affect naturally."vClient occasionally misunderstands implicit meanings in dialogue, and struggles to intuit the feelings of others."SStaff are advised to take a literal and direct approach when issuing commands."{Client is habitually docile and well-behaved, but reports enduring stress from day-to-day conflict in the environment."ÄClient also demonstrates a particular despondence in occasions where he feels unincluded-- indicative of sensitivity to neglect."ÉIt is likely that his awareness of the circumstances of his arrival to the facility contribute to a perceived sense of inferiority."ÑTREATMENT PLAN: Psychoanalytic talk therapy for the purpose of directly acknowledging repressed feelings of abandonment and neglect."[ECT has been used in exploration of the effects it might have on cognitive processing."Yes"No[[""Client Archive"",Unlocked the door with the Archive Key."Locked."@This is the Doctor's office. You're going to have to leave."#The Doctor will be displeased."!The Doctor does not approve.")Just what do you hope to accomplish?"You'll get nowhere."=I mean you might get somewhere literally, but, you know.""Lindsey Paraeah""
