imer Balls; 800 Dusk Balls"Continue reading?"çTransit Log: Stock: 6,000 Oran Berries; 4,000 Pecha Berries; 4,000 Chesto Berries; 4,000 Pomeg Berries; 5,000 Lum Berries; 100 Jaboca Berries"~Incident Record: A regular pitstop was made this afternoon at 3:15 PM in the Tourmaline Desert to service engine trouble."jAfter local wildlife endured a scuffle, the crew incidentally adopted one Pok√©mon Egg, now in cargo."3No issues expected with the Egg's acquisition."@It will be relinquished to company or personnel at request."IAnd a little bonus I picked up for my little girl back home in Orre."JIncident Record: An emergency stop was made this Tuesday at 11:53 PM."KAn unidentified railway obstruction has brought the vehicle to a halt."3Suspected fallen tree or other similar debris."IThough currently too dark to investigate, will do so in the morning."&Approx. projected delay: 8 hours."ZFriday 9:12 AM: I've identified the aforementioned obstruction, though it baffles me."BSpecifically, an entire tree has grown in the middle of rail."FI do not believe there is any such way that I can clear it alone."GAs such, I will be returning to Reborn City to request assistance."$Incident Record: Friday 1:37 PM"]In what I can only assume is an elaborate prank, I have failed to return to Reborn City."åAs I reversed the train down the same track which I had traveled just yesterday, I found a large portion of the rail to be missing entirely."ÉThe wood beams are scattered haplessly between the trees, and the metal has been contorted, and in some places, is absent entirely."lIn light of this, I am unable to move the freight at all, and will be returning to Reborn City on foot."ìIt should not take more than a day to reach the city, and assuming available resources, repairing the rail could be done in as little as two weeks."&Approx. projected delay: 18 days."Sunday 8:25 PM:"áIn the continuing saga of happenstances causing me to question my mental health, I have been unable to follow the track to Reborn City."^The scattered wood and disjointed metal I mentioned before was a dramatic understatement."9Entire segments of the track have been disapparated."êBetween the increasingly befuddling thickness of forestry and the baffling apparent deconstruction of the rail, I am unable to return to Reborn."éIn response to this distortion, I will follow the track on foot-- the only way in which it is (relatively) navigable, towards the Orre Region."JThough it is a considerable distance to walk, I see no second option."$Approx projected delay: 7 days."Monday 5:39 PM:"VIt appears I was hasty in my evaluation of the forward-going rail as 'navigable'."vThough I have ridden this way many times, I find the track going forward to be as distorted as it was going back."{These woods are mocking, with trees so in and out and roundabout such that one feels as if they've gone in circles forever."kIt was probably by luck that I stumbled upon this train again after having been lost in my expedition."4I'll continue searching for any sign of orient."`Thursday 7:18 PM: It's now been just about a full week since I was stranded in this forest."3Supplies in the train are diminishing quickly."fI find myself rationing more and I desperately hope to discover a source of berries in the woods."{It seems the Pok√©mon I obtained as a surprise for my daughter will have to be relegated to a gift of apology instead."&Approx. projected delay: Unknown."Saturday 1:20 AM:"oThis nightmarish place knows no logic, and yet I think that by a stroke of luck, I may have found the way."VWhile searching deep in among the woods, I spotted an opening I did not recogize."<As I followed it down a twisted path, I came to a cave."3The very cave through which the rail traveled!"@I recognized the stone, but strangely, I could see no rail."[Tomorrow I will gather what supplies I have left and quit this place once and for all."Sunday 11:20 PM:"[As if to taunt me with a glimpse of hope, I have not been successful in my evacuation."àThough I left early this morning, and searched again through every hour of the day, I was unable to locate the railcave from last night."|At this point, and with as little food as is left in this car, I will likely scarcely be able to make it to Orre alive."Wednesday 2:47 PM:"BTo my amazement, I once again found the same cave last night."0To my chagrin, I was unable to traverse it."@Though the rails linger inside the cave, they lead nowhere."TWhat I knew once as a sensible and one-directional tunnel now twists endlessly."ãAs if my entire life had been tossed into a kaleidoscope, I was unable to navigate the cave, and in fact, when I did finally find an exit--"9It turned out to be the very way in which I entered."&I've returned here for the night."I will try again tomorrow."Sunday 3:34 AM:"aWhen even finding the entrance to a cave proves difficult, traversing it appears impossible."QI have gone a precise way for these past few days, tracing my steps exactly."ÅBy now I have reliably found that although the path shifts, it is always through the southeast that I am able to stumble into it."RThe inside is maddening alone, however. This will require further expedition."Wednesday 7:44 PM:"NAfter exploring the cave and its nonsensical passages several times more,"äI have reliably found a path to a certain cove within the Railcave, and I plan to relocate my remaining supplies there as I press forward."qI will move forward as swiftly as possible with what little food is left, and my daughter's Pok√©mon in tow."FFor whoever may find this train, know the hardships I have faced.">Know, too, how you might escape these labyrinthine woods."fShould you find the Railcave, remember, the direction the rails move is no clue to traversing it."xBut as it may be, while they do not point you in the right direction, that appears to be all the guidance you need."Good luck, stranger."&This is the captain, signing out."0An Egg seems to have been abandoned here..."