 for any sign of orient."`Thursday 7:18 PM: It's now been just about a full week since I was stranded in this forest."3Supplies in the train are diminishing quickly."fI find myself rationing more and I desperately hope to discover a source of berries in the woods."{It seems the Pok√©mon I obtained as a surprise for my daughter will have to be relegated to a gift of apology instead."&Approx. projected delay: Unknown."Saturday 1:20 AM:"oThis nightmarish place knows no logic, and yet I think that by a stroke of luck, I may have found the way."VWhile searching deep in among the woods, I spotted an opening I did not recogize."<As I followed it down a twisted path, I came to a cave."3The very cave through which the rail traveled!"@I recognized the stone, but strangely, I could see no rail."[Tomorrow I will gather what supplies I have left and quit this place once and for all."Sunday 11:20 PM:"[As if to taunt me with a glimpse of hope, I have not been successful in my evacuation."àThough I left early this morning, and searched again through every hour of the day, I was unable to locate the railcave from last night."|At this point, and with as little food as is left in this car, I will likely scarcely be able to make it to Orre alive."Wednesday 2:47 PM:"BTo my amazement, I once again found the same cave last night."0To my chagrin, I was unable to traverse it."@Though the rails linger inside the cave, they lead nowhere."TWhat I knew once as a sensible and one-directional tunnel now twists endlessly."ãAs if my entire life had been tossed into a kaleidoscope, I was unable to navigate the cave, and in fact, when I did finally find an exit--"9It turned out to be the very way in which I entered."&I've returned here for the night."I will try again tomorrow."Sunday 3:34 AM:"aWhen even finding the entrance to a cave proves difficult, traversing it appears impossible."QI have gone a precise way for these past few days, tracing my steps exactly."ÅBy now I have reliably found that although the path shifts, it is always through the southeast that I am able to stumble into it."RThe inside is maddening alone, however. This will require further expedition."Wednesday 7:44 PM:"NAfter exploring the cave and its nonsensical passages several times more,"äI have reliably found a path to a certain cove within the Railcave, and I plan to relocate my remaining supplies there as I press forward."qI will move forward as swiftly as possible with what little food is left, and my daughter's Pok√©mon in tow."FFor whoever may find this train, know the hardships I have faced.">Know, too, how you might escape these labyrinthine woods."fShould you find the Railcave, remember, the direction the rails move is no clue to traversing it."xBut as it may be, while they do not point you in the right direction, that appears to be all the guidance you need."Good luck, stranger."&This is the captain, signing out."0An Egg seems to have been abandoned here..."Take it?"\PN got the Egg!"Yes"No0Iu;␀ê[[\"/This rock is glowing with energy inside...""Do you want to mine the rock?",It seems too sturdy to break or move..."UThe rock base may hold more valuables. Do you want to open it with Blast Powder?"\PN found an EEVEE!""Captain's Log""Should you read this?"Day unknown."EI've been unsuccessful thus far in navigating this hellish cave."Despite the rails--"5Despite the stone markings I've tried to leave--"ADespite carefully recording my passages through this place--"I'm baffled."Utterly and completely..."TI felt relocating here would be a leap towards progress to finding my way home."GInstead I feel I've entrenched myself in the prison of this place."Continue reading?">Progress has once again teased me with her coy seduction."ÉIn my continual stumbling through the labyrinth, I found nestled into the wall, a door imprinted upon the stone in a glowing light."HBeyond its threshold, a world of glittering, static blue and stars."/I do not know what awaits me in the world."I do know that I am weak."BI am thin, and exhausted-- physically, mentally, emotionally."AI cannot refuse the chance that this will lead me to safety."RBut there is no promise in those jilted lands, and I do not expect to return."If anyone finds this--"6Please apologize to my little girl, Snow, for me."@And her gift-- I would ask someone look after the Pok√©mon."PI may disappear into this strange dimension, but it need not share my fate."+This is Captain Florence, signing out."Good night."+\PN obtained Field Effect Read-Out 37!"+Info on Psychic Terrain now available!"ARC: You're just in time."ARC: Hey, \PN."%Though I'd join you on this one,"5Given the nature of who we're dealing with here.""???: And you're the Champion.":And you've been working with the cops, is that right?"LGotta say, I never imagined the likes of me comin' to someone like you."AARCLIGHT: Do you mean you're the one who sent in the report?".An illegal poacher, asking for city help?"#???: And you must be Arclight."Name's Breslin."!I'll try to keep this short:"XMe and my gang were commissioned to help acquire a valuable Electric-Type Pok√©mon."ARCLIGHT: "Acquire.""$BRESLIN: Standard work, really."But this commissioner..."GShe seems to care very little about what happens to me or my crew."[ARCLIGHT: Surely you're used to taking a few risks, operating outside the law and all."!BRESLIN: It's not only that."$She seems a little... unhinged."]It's got to the point that I don't care what happens to her, or even if we get our cut--"We're out."It's too dangerous."&And that's where you two come in."-I can lead you right to her and my team,"CAll I ask is a little protection from the long arm of the law."What do you say?"BRESLIN: Good."0Let's put a stop to whatever her plans are."ARC: We'll help,"6But I'm not promising any form of legal immunity."BRESLIN: I get it."5Should've known better than to trust a Champion."Let alone a cop."2ARC: We can't guarantee you any "protection".">You still hav