 titter!"NOEL: ...Perhaps."RADOMUS: No haps about it!",'Twas a snicker, a snirtle-- a twitter!"NOEL: Dad--"DRADOMUS: And what starts with a smirk may evolve past a 'snrk',"2Into a jeer, a fleer-- maybe a hearty guffaw!"3Once a chortle, a chuckle-- someday a hee-haw!"KA machination of cachinnation-- Crackling, cackling, a massive howl..."7To grin, gibe and giggle-- and laugh jowl to jowl!"!NOEL: Hahah, okay already..."=RADOMUS: You've lived too much to have smiled so little."ZPlease forgive your old man for taking pleasure in every snort he can fleece you for."9NOEL: You said your father used to take you fishing." Will you tell me about him?"RADOMUS: With pleasure.")RADOMUS: Where to start, I wonder..."XHis name was as much a fiction as my own, but for quite different reasons entirely."Yes"No;[ü"(???: Hello challenger, and welcome."Please, follow me.""LUNA: Gardevoir! You're back!"'GARDEVOIR: But of course, my dear~"#LUNA: Oh, how I've missed you!"?Now don't you go off disappearing like that again, please."GARDEVOIR: Pish posh~"?What's a girl without a little excitement in her life, hm?"SBesides, I had my Gallade-in-shining-armor come all the way down to rescue me!"BRADOMUS: There was hardly much rescuing involved, but indeed."+The perceived crisis has been averted.",LUNA: Oh, Master, you are so wonderful!"*I am pleased to be in service to you."9RADOMUS: Now, now. Let's not get ahead of ourselves."I am but a humble Gallade."OCAIN: Speaking of which, why do you keep changing to all these silly hats?"RADOMUS: You wound me."&There's nothing silly about them."#But to answer your question..."Why not?">RADOMUS: I simply choose the right hat for the right job."Isn't that sensible?"^GARDEVOIR: I'm afraid the peasantry knows nothing of my master's divine taste in fashion."8LUNA: I find them most amusing. Don't you think so?"fRADOMUS: Yes, well, speaking of nonsequitur transitions, I have somebody to introduce to you all."3If you would be so kind as to step asi