Here."You go here."And then the bishop."RADOMUS: ...";...No, no, I can move here instead on the turn before."NOEL: Knight."RADOMUS: ...Blast."JNOEL: A more accurate play would be to push this pawn the turn prior."%RADOMUS: How did you see that..."*NOEL: It's not a matter of seeing it."!It's a matter of knowing it."?Just because you can't see it doesn't mean it's not there."RADOMUS: ...Indeed."You see how amazing he is?"I told you."!NOEL: It's not that amazing."çRADOMUS: Well, look here-- I only may be a Grandmaster through forged records and stolen identity, but neither am I quite so near the bottom."eThe fact that you so consistently wipe the proverbial floor with me is nothing to be sneezed at."Your sister, too."Every time."BYou appear to have inherited a talent even I never possessed."(Must be your mother's, I suppose..."I had no idea."&Do you kids ever play each other?"NOEL: We used to.".There wasn't much to do at the orphanage." Now there are more options."@RADOMUS: And to think I asked for your help to beat Anna..."3Perhaps I should ask for her help to beat you."$NOEL: So it was just about her?"@RADOMUS: On the contrary, you are the one I'm playing with."ITo ask for your help was simply an excuse to pass the time together."NOEL: Right."-RADOMUS: It isn't the most elegant play,";But then, some fathers make their children go fishing."3I can't imagine you'd care for that very much."I certainly never did..."%This seemed much more palatable."Was I wrong?"NOEL: I don't know.")Chess isn't very interesting either."RADOMUS: Isn't it?"GNOEL: There's a finite number of moves that can be made each turn."It's calculable."8And with modern AI, it's practically a solved game."#RADOMUS: Well, I suppose so..."I'll do better next then."NOEL: It's fine."I don't really mind."!...Father, what is this hat?"!RADOMUS: Ah, can't you tell?";I have to try hard to even stand a chance against you,"*So naturally, I wore my thinking cap!"NOEL: ...Snrk."RADOMUS: Aha! A titter!"NOEL: ...Perhaps."RADOMUS: No haps about it!",'Twas a snicker, a snirtle-- a twitter!"NOEL: Dad--"DRADOMUS: And what starts with a smirk may evolve past a 'snrk',"2Into a jeer, a fleer-- maybe a hearty guffaw!"3Once a chortle, a chuckle-- someday a hee-haw!"KA machination of cachinnation-- Crackling, cackling, a massive howl..."7To grin, gibe and giggle-- and laugh jowl to jowl!"!NOEL: Hahah, okay already..."=RADOMUS: You've lived too much to have smiled so little."ZPlease forgive your old man for taking pleasure in every snort he can fleece you for."9NOEL: You said your father used to take you fishing." Will you tell me about him?"RADOMUS: With pleasure.")RADOMUS: Where to start, I wonder..."XHis name was as much a fiction as my own, but for quite different reasons entirely."Yes"NoIu;␀8/[[R"PThrough the binoculars, a waterfall can be seen pouring down into the city."%An elegant cabin rests above it."DThrough the binoculars, a small cabin in the woods can be seen."'A Pikachu is sitting on top of it."JThrough the binoculars, a small city can be seen on the cliffs above."DThere's no activity whatsoever. The streets are entirely empty."[It seems to be bustling with people out and about! The streets are livelier than ever.">This center is the local extension of a breeding project."|Using samples raised by the Breeding Center on Azurine Island, we work day and night to restore the wild Pok√©mon to Reborn!"QWe're happy to be productively communicating with our sister facility again!"fAlthough we haven't heard from the Azurine Center in quite a while. I do hope nothing's happened."]This center is for wildlife research and the preservation of Pok√©mon species in nature."RWe keep close watch on the natural activity of all the Pok√©mon in this area."ZMany of the Pok√©mon around here are in constant competition. It's quite interesting!"eTauros and Bouffalant constantly butt heads- literally- for dominance over the Miltank and land."YEven in the forests, many Bug-types will engage each other for control of resources."@Ultimately, we seek to restore equilibrium to the region..."QBut perhaps we shouldn't have introduced these species to the area together."ôGiven the constant conflict among the wild Pok√©mon, we've observed that the Pok√©mon tend to be thankful to those who help them overcome their opponent."kFor instance, the Tauros here will even be so kind as to allow a human who helps them to ride on them!"bOur studies show that Bouffalant tend to be the most standoffish of the Pok√©mon around here."5They have a tendency to charge about uncaringly."pIn fact, when they do so, they often neglect to steer and end up crashing into or displacing other objects."LTauros will sometimes let Trainers ride them. It's quite an experience!"AThey move swiftly and will even jump up ledges effortlessly."However, they are still finnicky creatures. Tauros greatly dislike going through very tall grass with a human riding them."vOur current hypothesis is that the grass somehow disrupts their balance, but it could just be sheer stubbornness."mMany of the Pok√©mon in the forests are drawn to the scent of Honey produced by the Combee in the woods."ÉSo popular is this nectar that Pok√©mon with a particular taste for it-- Heracross and Pinsir-- will often fight each other for it."\We've attempted to capture some of the Bug-types in the forest to study them further..."^But when they're engaged in combat with each other, it seems they're impossible to catch."\Their focus is honed to the point that they can easily deflect any Ball. Unfortunate..."=We keep track of the Miltank here for breeding purposes."hAfter all, we don't want the population to spiral; we're just trying to keep it in balance for now."|Miltank produce milk very slowly normally, but given proper diet and conditioning, the process can be sped up exponentially."çOur Miltank prefer and are conditioned to an Oran diet- that is, Oran Berries. Consequently, when given one, they produce their milk rapidly."`Reborn's environment has been desecrated, so there's no longer many places to grow Berries."7The forests around here are a bit of an exception."=If you find a spot to grow Berries, feel free to use it."\On another note, there are also a variety of sundries that have been lost in this area."RWe never mind passersby cleaning up, so if you find something, help yourself."9To that tune, you might find this to be of some use."JDad-gum it, I dropped my glasses while doing research in the woods..."UIt's a miracle I made it out of that stupid forest-maze, but now what will I do?"&\PN handed over the Tech Glasses."5By golly, that's them! Miracles rain down on me!"SOops, maybe I shouldn't make talk of miracles in a studious place like this..."%Anyway, why don't you take this?"8\PN obtained a Department Store Sticker: Heracross!"AHm? I see you don't have a Department Store Membership Card."HShould you choose to get one, please come back to me for a Sticker."Why don't you take this?">Now to get back to work... or find another excuse not to."^Did you know there's a certain Pok√©mon that evolves only when you want it NOT to evolve?"Ain't that crazy?"tThis is the kinda stuff I live for! Now we need to figure out why it does that here and not in other regions..."@Ah, hello again. Have you come to donate a Dunsparce to us?"`The Azurine Center has been beyond tardy in their shipments of Pok√©mon for reintroduction."oWe were scheduled to re-establish the Dunsparce population last month, but there's been no word from them."tIt is a poor substitute, but, Trainer, should you encounter any Dunsparce, please consider donating them to us."çI will offer you a young Pok√©mon in return. We had planned to reintroduce them to the wild before, but were forced to cancel that operation."I understand."1I see. This will be a great boon, thank you."&\PN traded DUNSPARCE for TYROGUE!"XThis will be an excellent addition to the populations' re-establishment. Thank you."CAh, are you trying to make your way through the local forests?"$You'll find this to be helpful."MIf you need more, you can buy them a certain flower shop in Reborn City,"oOr otherwise one of the oddballs who lives in the woods here can sometimes be convinced to part with some."SIf you need more honey, you can buy them a certain flower shop in Reborn City,"Ugggh, I got a job here as an intern, but putting together data on the environment is way less interesting than I thought!"hI thought I'd be out touching the grass, but here I am, cranking away on application development..."SWhen they asked me for a password, I should've just told them "allfieldapp"..."kIf I'd done that, I wouldn't have had to bother collecting information on things like Field Effects..."\I could just lay down in the grass and become one with the earth like I was meant to..."Yes"No[R"PThrough the binoculars, a waterfall can be seen pouring down into the city."%An elegant cabin rests above it."DThrough the binoculars, a small cabin in the woods can be seen."'A Pikachu is sitting on top of it."JThrough the binoculars, a small city can be seen on the cliffs above."DThere's no activity whatsoever. The streets are entirely empty."[It seems to be bustling with people out and about! The streets are livelier than ever.">This center is the local extension of a breeding project."|Using samples raised by the Breeding Center on Azurine Island, we work day and night to restore the wild Pok√©mon to Reborn!"QWe're happy to be productively communicating with our sister facility again!"fAlthough we haven't heard from the Azurine Center in quite a while. I do hope nothing's happened."]This center is for wildlife research and the preservation of Pok√©mon species in nature."RWe keep close watch on the natural activity of all the Pok√©mon in this area."ZMany of the Pok√©mon around here are in constant competition. It's quite interesting!"eTauros and Bouffalant constantly butt heads- literally- for dominance over the M