hile. There's something fishy about it, yanno."oAnd I've seen you buy from this guy a few times, yeah? But you don't seem like his typical customer to me."???: Hey, you. Come here."{Who are you? I've been keeping my eye on this place for a while, but you don't seem like this guy's typical customer to me."\PN, huh?"aWell, I'm Arclight- DJ Arclight, to be specific. I run the Nightclub up in the Obsidia Ward."&You can just call me Arc. Anyway."YI'm pretty sure that these Pok√©mon he's selling are stolen, and I ain't about that."_Most of his customers don't care a thing about Pok√©mon. They usually end up abusing them."íIf these Pok√©mon really are stolen, it's probably hopeless to find their original owners, but, I figure at least we can get them to a good place."3And I'm thinkin' you might be that good place."èSo I'll tell you what, \PN, I'm gonna leave it to you to buy up the rest of these guys. He won't sell to me; I've raised hell here in the past."MAnd once we've cleaned his stock, then I'll bust in and clean his clock."CMake sure this guy gets shut down for good. Sound like a plan?"I'm countin' on you."ARC: Yo. \PN."ïIf these Pok√©mon really are stolen, it might not be practical to find their original owners, but, I figure at least we can get them to a good place."&Huh, you already did it? Not bad." Looks like you did it, huh?"wI owe you one, for sure. I can rest a bit easier knowing that those Pok√©mon will be taken care of no matter what."FIt might not be a bad idea to hang onto them just in case though."ëAs for that guy... I won't do anything out in the open. But let me put it this way-- Next time you're around here, don't expect to see him again."1Anyway, here's a little 'thank you' from me." Do what you will with that."<If you ever get into the Nightclub, hit me up for sure!"ÜCRAUDBURRY: Miserable lout, PATHETIC inventory, if this is really all you've got, you ought to be ashamed of your scruffy-rumped self!"=Don't call again until you have something worth my time!"CRAUDBURRY: Oh, it's you."RI shoulda known I'd see low-life scum like you lollygagging around down here."kDon't look at me, criminal swine, you aren't worth my breath! Drivelling mucus with every step... Bah!"7ARCHER: Quite the mouth that one has, doesn't she?"6MAXWELL: You gonna let her talk to you like that?"cARCHER: Perhaps unfortunately, the street-savvy aren't the only ones with influence down here."èThere's always people like Craudburry. She pretends to be such an upstanding citizen, but she just plays the streets down here with her wealth."dYou recall the Pok√©mon we stole from her, yes? That was one she purchased illegally down here."2That's why I had no regrets in targeting her."WNonetheless, her attitude is insufferable. Yet, no one down here stands up to her."1After all, they dare not risk her patronage."xI'm thinking, though, perhaps we might better everyone's lives down here if we, how do you say, teach her a lesson?"4If you're interested, find me around her house."NMAXWELL: I'll tell you what, that broad has way too much power down here."}This is supposed to be place for the strong to survive, not for some rich bitch to order everyone around as she pleases."SBut that's just it. Money casts a powerful curse. And she gets what she wants."$Like stolen Pok√©mon. You know?"]That's why I tried to take it back from her before. She didn't even play fair to get it."YMost people don't dare stand up to someone like her-- they might lose their squeeze."But us? We're different."AKnow what I mean? I think we oughta teach that one a lesson."<Come find me around her house. We'll settle this score."For, you know, glory."DEFACTO: Well met, \PN."1Do tell, how do you find business down here?"~Personally, I manage to make a pretty penny, but it can be a veritable struggle to reason with some of these lesser merchants."pSee, the economy down here-- as with any underworld market-- works on a separate axis of supply and demand."KOne singular substance reigns supreme here: "Rare Candy". Heard of it?"èWell, perhaps it is best that someone like you never does. For many of these fellows, however, they are already too addicted to the "level up"."8Incidentally, do you know how "Rare Candy" is made?"ìBy distilling the synthetic compounds of other items-- specifically Crystal Shards and Heart Scales-- one is left with a highly reactive substance."eCombined with the traditional medicinal Pok√©mon Rare Candy, a violent psychoactive is produced."gBut, as such, it is these ingredients which are in high demand down here: Shards and Heart Scales."XThus, it is extremely beneficial for those able to gather these resources to do so."This is where I come in!"]I have a brand new product that can help the crafty geologist maximize their efficiency."1Blast Powder is a unique reactive substance."òWhen placed on certain kinds of damaged rock-- the glowing sediment I'm sure you've seen-- it will allow previously harvested spots to become lucrative."3In short, it allows you to mine a stone twice.""That established... Buy some!"8DEFACTO: You return! Come to buy more Blast Powder?"VBREAK: Oh, \PN! Do stay a moment, I have an amazing discovery to regale you with!"WAlthough this is 7th Street, some find it more like a 7th Heaven. Do you know why?"COh, I shall tell you. It's because they're out of their minds!"Literally~"8Do tell, do tell, have you ever tried "Rare Candy"?"FOh, I suspect you haven't-- it's not what you feed your Pok√©mon."/This is a very special kind of "level up"."6But I will tell you the ingredients of the thing!"SUGAR!"SPICE!"And EVERYTHING NICE!"Just kidding."ÇActually it's the benzoylmethylecgonine dust and crystal-isomerized piperonyl acetone embedded in Heart Scales and crystal Shards."lThen you stick that in a normal Rare Candy and you'll be partyin' it up, down, sideways AND diagonally."HAnyway, it turns out Heart Scales and Shards are useful to collect."3Not always easy though! They play hard to get."*By hiding in hard things, like rocks."0Sure, you can mine some out, but then what?"xI'll tell you what! Then you take some Blast Powder and blow up the base of the rock so you can mine even MORE out!"LThen you sell them and become king of the world! Or queen. Or whatever.";Anyway yes, Blast Powder! Mine things twice! Buy some!"ABREAK: Blast Powder! More fun than exploding chocolate cake!"Merry mining~!""DEFACTO: You're back at last!";Might I interest you in a fresh stock of Blast Powder?"ÇOh, please refrain from invoking any of that platitudinous job-seeking discourse that the boss has been so intent on spouting off."cAs his analytical holiness refuses to acknowledge, I am already gainfully employed right here."'As such, why not indulge yourself?"gDEFACTO: Admittedly, it might have been a boon to be in a slightly more intellectual line of work."ïKnowledge is the seat of personal growth, but aside from which downcast countenaces are the most likely customers, there's little to be learned here."YBut that anything like that would exist in this city is a far cry. I'm content here."9BREAK: \PN! My old friend and most valued customer~!"FListen! We've got a problemo in the gang and his name is Maxwell."QBut the way he's talking about breaking us up, we oughta call him Maxunwell!";Ohoh, don't look at me like that. It's spine-tingling."pMore seriously, I can't think of a job better suited to my talents than synthesizing benzoylmethylecgonine."0Most people can't even pronounce that word."It's a gift."ìI suppose I am familiar with a variety of chemical, herbal and questionably legal substances that might be handy to those with bizarre interests..."BBut really, no one these days likes to think outside the box.",So we might as well just blow stuff up!"fRemember, if it doesn't seem like a good idea, that just means you're not using enough sparklers."?You Aqua punks still struttin' around like you're so cool?"#Hmph. Not like it matters now."|Please, your blank stare is piercing into my soul. I cannot possibly exist under the pressure of your black-pixel eyes."JEven in its death-- I will show you the true POWER of the Magma Gang!"You are strong indeed."6Hoo-hah. I bow to a strength greater than my own.";I'm not letting the Aqua Gang go down without a fight!"Too strong."WMan, how many Rare Candies did you feed YOUR Pok√©mon? All of mine weren't enough!"Send out your Pok√©mon."...Understood."%You have no need to speak to me."DOh, man. I like what I'm seein'. You? You look like fresh meat."7Ugh, I was the one who got chewed up and spit out."7Lesson learned, don't judge the book by its cover."eDude... The Butterfree are soooo like lackadaisical. They totally just morphed into that beam..."$Aha, yah, wha? What's going on?"Duuuuuuude..."8Dude. I'm sooo fuckin' leveled right now. Fight me!"Woaaaaah..."Like, shit. Shiiiiiit."@Dude. You new around here? I don't think I seen you before."6LOL, I'm just messin' with you man. How are you?!"JIt's been a while! Man, remember last time we dropped Candy together?"0...Wait, you mean you really don't know me?".Shit dude, you're not with them, are you?"<I don't trust you. I never seen you around here before.":You're obviously a cop in disguise! Get away from me!"MI don't know why my boyfriend insists on selling down here all the time."!All these men are so creepy.",Bro, you got any "Rare Candy" to spare?"'Heh... 'Spare Candy'. That's good.""Hey, you got a problem, bud?!"8You think I steal from you? I ain't steal from you!"3If you gotta problem, let's go! You wanna go?!"Fuck, dude.">What the hell, dude. You can have your shit back, christ.":Fuck me, you looked like an easy pick, too... Dammit."#Stow it, I'll leave you alone."7Dude, you wanna give me some cash? I need a fix..."lSome people was worried that the fuzz would bust this place up if it was found during the construction."Hah! We show 'em."*Incompetent police don't have a clue!"F7th Street is the one place that won't change! This is OUR world!"N