y charge."uThough on his command, through inaction I've allowed ruin to befall the very bloodline I was sworn to safeguard."3There is much legacy that has been my undoing,"QAnd it is this which will hang over my conscience for all my days remaining."lI pray my services elsewhere are enough to give purpose and life to an otherwise wholly failed steward."And, should they not be,"^That I can live up to his final command fully enough that he would not have regretted it.""Leave," he said."&"Go do whatever makes you happy.""!"Is that an order?" I asked."He affirmed."IThough generous, I believe it was an order not born from generosity."Rather, desperation."4He perhaps wanted me to have what he could not."OBut could he now-- if he were here to outlive the conflict of his lineage?"???: --fInd oUT.",LUNA: Pardon? Did you... say something?"???: I wanT-- to fInd oUT!"TAKA: I wanT oUT."LUNA: Young Master...?"TAKA: I'm-- aliVE."I feeL-- aliVE."LUNA: Is it truly..."ATAKA: ThesE wrEtched haLLwayS' stAle aIr neVer felT so goOD.")I wanT to burN iT alL to the groUND."#OuR histoRy haS alReadY endED."$Let'S senD thiS prisOn wiTH iT."6LUNA: You are possessed of this malignant energy."TAKA: It'S noT so bAD."CLUNA: Essence of the New World, tainted by a virulent creator."SIt is bound to bring out the most destructive sides of those whom it envelops."TAKA: DesTructive?"No-- I feeL greAT."$I don'T wanT to leT go oF thiS.")FoR the firsT timE-- seaRinG desIRE."
