me see it?"#Mmm. Right, so see this crack?"RIt was probably dropped from a long way up or something. That doesn't matter."ôThe problem is, if some debris gets through the exterior into the circuits, then it can distort the electric transmission, and then-- well, this happens."`It might not be impossible to fix, but you're honestly better off just buying another ball."^DESIGNER: You're determined to fix this ball? It probably won't be usable no matter what."HThere is the chance that a Pok√©mon was inside at one point, but..."åWell, when inside Pok√© Balls, lifeforce data of Pok√©mon is converted to a digital format. Meaning the Pok√©mon itself can corrupt as well."FWhatever this originally was before, it's probably Missingno now."EMissingno can't be caught or tamed, so there's no point to that."+Are you sure you still want to fix it?"DESIGNER: I see."eI have an old diagnostic kit with me, let me see if I can detect any lingering data in the ball."..."......"........."1Mm... The data corruption is already at 96%."?This is probably useless, but let's see what we can use..."Ah, Magnet Powder."wThat will be small enough to slip inside the crack. Then, there's a chance that can reboot the internal circuitry."2Of course, it might also erase the circuitry."LBut we don't have a better option, given the conditions. It's a gamble."*DESIGNER: That's the sensible choice.">It's always sad when broken balls have to be thrown away."DESIGNER: You brought Magnet Powder, I see. Well, I can't say I don't admire your commitment, but it's probably pointless."&Anyway, let's see what we can do.""The corruption is at 98% now."]Are you prepared to defeat the Missingno inside? It would be problematic to let it free."+DESIGNER: All right, if you're sure..."Let's do it this way."ûDESIGNER: Magnet Powder is in... It's going to juggle the circuits a bit, and with any luck, there will be a second where the ball 'forgets' that it's broken."6Either that or the data will be deleted entirely