s, this region's technology is practically stone age."cIf you saw what we're used to back where I'm from, you wouldn't even know what to think of it."PAll I need is a living example to confirm, and I've practically cracked it."MEVE: If you're confident that you can solve it, I'll cooperate with you."FLORA: It's not an "if"."!Glad to hear we have a deal."DAnyway, \PN, it looks like you're not needed here, so good-bye!"%EVE: Actually, that's incorrect."1We'll be needing \PN's help from the outset."FLORA: Excuse me?"6EVE: You said you wanted a living PULSE specimen."There's one left."3It was somehow completed without my knowledge."EFLORA: Hmph. Maybe I should've found whoever did that instead..." EVE: Good luck. She's dead."$EVE: Good luck. She's gone now."FLORA: ...Tch."So where is it?"&EVE: It's in the Champion's room."FLORA: ..."You're kidding, right?"That's a joke."EVE: It's what I've heard."FLORA: ...Fine."+FLORA: Then I'm going to Charous Hall."IThat's where the Pok√©mon League is in this miserable region, right?"8Meet me there and our deal for Magearna is back on."4But you better not fuck this up for me. Got it?"EVE: She seems pleasant.":I recognize that this is an unideal situation, but..."#Lumi's clock is still ticking."IIf there's something we can do to further her odds, then I'll do it."No questions asked."3Just this once, I'm asking you to do the same."-Please help Flora, \PN. For Lumi's sake."FEVE: Please help Flora reach the last PULSE in the Champion Room."_Returning to our bodies is wonderful, but it just means that Lumi's time is limited again."'This may finally be a way forward.",FLORA: I guess that's about everything."-Your cooperation is greatly appreciated~"And don't worry."kUnlike some people, I'll be making sure from the get go that the Pok√©mon aren't hurt by my creations."4EVE: You can stop with the guilt trips already."3FLORA: I just hope you've learned your lesson!"0EVE: Your findings were admittedly helpful."•Splitting the excess energy among several individuals of the same species certainly could act as a bandaid solution until we can solve the problem of over- exposure."0It's an intelligent and effective solution."7FLORA: Oh, I love it when they praise me properly."SEVE: ...But, as I was about to say, your attitude is well beyond insufferable."Good bye."FLORA: Hmph!"0Don't be too hasty to push me out the door!"CAfter all, I still have my half of the deal to uphold for \PN."JFLORA: Magearna is still in the Glass Workstation, near where we met."It's on the second level."eI went ahead and set up a ladder so you can reach it, so don't say I never did anything for you."óI would've gone after it myself, but there was so much trash in the way, and that glowy aura around it looked a whole lot like somebody ELSE's problem."$So, you're welcome or whatever."I'd say it's been a treat,"SBut if it were, it'd be the kind that makes your stomach hurt after eating it."Ta."?EVE: I do hope she doesn't do anything we'll regret later.":Despite herself though, she has opened a door for me."6There's much work to do again, and time is short."/Please forgive me for not staying to chat."+Best of luck dealing with the Anomaly.Iu;␀H[[G",A switch on the machine opens the case."Press it?"Who wouldn't?"Better not..."HEATHER: ..."...Stupid Blake."Stupid Dad..."Stupid Mom..."(Why did you have to leave me alone?"..."I'm so sick of this..."I'm always alone."2HEATHER: If it's not one thing, it's another." Stupid Blake with his lies!","Oh sure, Heather! I'll look after you."KYou can crash with me and we don't even have to have any rules at all!"#You can do whatever you want!""1Yeah, and I'll be locked up in a cage, LIAR!"LThe only crashing we'll do is when I crash your face into the ground..."Stupid jerk."("This is the crag of life, Heather."/All will break themselves on it, in time."")Is that why you joined Team Meteor?!"'To betray me and break me faster?!"X"You should have known better than to expec