Look."hSIMON: Not that I could get her body out of the lake, but I figured she at least deserved a memory.",I couldn't even find out her last name."6I don't know if she had any family, or friends..."5All of that rests at the bottom of the lake now.";SIMON: I swore that I would get revenge on that woman."$But what good is another death?"\Someone, somewhere, must feel the same about that woman as I did for Tara... and Lyssa."Twice now."$Twice, I lost the girl I loved."KWhen my wife died, I could think of nothing else but getting her back." Then Commander Sirius came."ZHe told me when Team Meteor recreated the world anew, that I could have my wife back."#I was all too happy to accept."[But then I was partnered with Tara, and she was always so energetic and sincere and..."%I fell in love with her instead."#She was the light of my world."&Now I'm left with darkness again."HDo you think, if the world was reborn, I would see them both again?""SIMON: You're probably right."6But then what? How could I explain that to Lyssa?"5Even in redemption, all that awaits me is guilt."SIMON: ...Of course not.";It was all just a pipe dream to begin with, wasn't it?"DRunning away from this world was just a way to escape my guilt." Guilt for losing my wife...",Guilt from not dying in Tara's place..."NGuilt for having felt anything for Tara after I swore my life to Lyssa..."<Even if I saw them again, I couldn't bear to face them."$I'm resigning from Team Meteor."6I've spent too long dwelling on the past already."I can't take it anymore."@There's no point in trying to recreate what's already lost."NIf you ever need to find me, I'll be at my home in the west Peridot Ward.""Lyssa Copperman""*...\PN's Soul Candle suddenly lights!""The pumpkin begins to glow..."%The name is too mangled to read."9"Officer Jacob S. Crowley -Passed in recent service"",VICTORIA: Oh! \PN, are you really back?"YI've heard about a lot of things happening up in Carnelia, and I was really worried!"%But of course, you