nia Drastic Measures Andersen.""WShe used to play bass when we were younger, so I thought she could help teach Aya,"TAnd believe me, I got a few drastic measures in my ear about it already myself."+But I've got faith in 'em both, yanno?"It'll go great!"dGettin' to do this has been on my bucket list for a while, so I ain't lettin' the chance slide."IOnly thing slidin' around here's gonna be my guitar, mark the words."EBut I gotta focus still, so I'll see you once the curtain drops!"'...The proverbial curtain, anyway.".HARDY: And like, da-da-dada ba, ba, ba..."Nah, let's try..."!Da-da dada, baaayaaayaaaa..."AYA: Like this..."And this..."And..."-...Tch, was it the second or third fret?"TITANIA: Third."8AYA: Ugh. I'm never going to remember this in time."SEspecially not while also having to worry about performing in front of people."'Like, real, actual human people..."5I should just sit out before I embarrass myself."#TITANIA: Nope, you're in this."rI don't agree with my idiot brother putting you in front of a crowd as one of your first experiences playing,"6And your idiot brother's not off the hook either,"<But if you quit now, I'll have entirely wasted my time,"KMore importantly, if you're going to quit, do it because you want out,"8Not because you're afraid of failing on the way in."1If you do that, you'll never learn anything."AYA: I'm beginning to think that the entire known world is conspiring to get me to make as big of a fool of myself as possible."FIf that's what you all want, I can just go apply to Agate Circus."(I'm sure they're hiring new clowns."(At least I'd get paid for it there."6TITANIA: I'm not here to be your therapist, girl."&Cut the fatalistic act and focus,",Otherwise you can practice on your own."$AYA: Geez, I was just joking..."8TITANIA: Tell a joke you wouldn't actually believe.")Now get back to it; clock's ticking."(AYA: It's been like this all day..."+Hardy conned me into playing with him."<It sounded fun until I got here and saw all t