e, Rock Type is your only viable choice to hit Dragonite effectively."HTry to save such an attacker for it to reduce its chances to sweep."&If anyone can win this, it's you."PThis is your final hurdle before properly claiming your championship title!"AI'll be off now, to see what difference I can make up there."Best of luck, Champion."7No one seems to be picking up at the Grand Hall..."*SAPHIRA: Welcome to home, sweet home."In a sense."0T3RR4: N44444444WH B1SH, TH1S MY H0USE NA0."II, THE K1NG OF EV1L, HAVE CLA1MED THIS SACR3D G0LDEN LAND AS MY OWN!"2AND W1TH IT, ALL Y0UR b00ty ARE B3LONG TO US!""RAWWWWWWWWWWRRRRRRR!!!!!!!!!!"ESAPHIRA: And now, I'll show you the best thing about this place."-INTERCOM VOLUME MUTED-"bSAPHIRA: This gym was built inside the competitive facility for convenience and broadcasting."jBut it would be annoying if a concurrent tournament's announcements played over a private gym battle."<This way, we can make sure challenges stay undisturbed."DI can't imagine being more thankful for it than I am right now.")SAPHIRA: I'll be waiting at the top,"4But there are things you must understand first."+SAPHIRA: What is most precious to you?"\SAPHIRA: Nothing in the world is more important that an emotion that only you can feel."1Isn't that just another form of selfishness?"(SAPHIRA: But you chose this anyway."BSAPHIRA: There's nothing wrong with striving for inner peace."cIf you could take a pill that made you feel at peace forever, with no side-effects, would you?"CSAPHIRA: Because you don't think you can find it in the world."AYou give up a fight that no living man is permitted to quit."<SAPHIRA: Then happiness itself is not what's important."4What's important is your struggle to attain it."@SAPHIRA: To favor that is to lose the forest for the trees."DCurrency is only as valuable as what else you could do with it."2It is a tool to maintain freedom and control."2Isn't there another way to find those things?"3SAPHIRA: But still you chose to focus on coin."XDid you lack faith in your ability to reach that freedom, or did you just not care?"3SAPHIRA: To be alive is to fight for survival."(To be human is to know inferiority."*Even the confident will still perish."LIsn't that just what you told yourself so you never had to risk trying?"bIn the end, you choose to buy that freedom with money instead of creating it inside yourself." That's the expensive route."\Isn't it ironic how you force yourself to lose the thing you said you cared about most?"*All because you didn't want to fight."*SAPHIRA: And how did you decide that?"@One never knows if a lock matches a key until they open it."8Either the lock is sprung, or they give up looking."cDid you just convince yourself you had exhausted all your options to justify your resignation?"lSAPHIRA: Because in the end, the illusion of freedom was more important to you than actually having it."<You are unwilling to fight, but unwilling to surrender."That is your purgatory."DSAPHIRA: It can't be done because you decided it can't be done."*That is the power of your conviction."eThat proves that you already have everything you need to cultivate that freedom within yourself."sYou just choose not to use it because you'd rather blame your shortcomings on an economy rather than yourself."?You don't lack the ability to fight; only the backbone to."KSAPHIRA: Which is more important, your value to them or theirs to you?"9SAPHIRA: Do you really believe you're that selfless?"PHaving value to others is just a roundabout way of keeping yourself secure.".Are you sure you even have value to them?"1SAPHIRA: To be human is to know inferiority."hCertainty is never just that-- only a point at which we've decided to stop pursuing a deeper truth."!It's when you stop fighting."\So you don't even know if the thing that's allegedly most important to you even exists."+But still you stood there and said it.".So, you're just fighting to make it true?"8So what really matters is what they can do for you." Aren't you just using them?"WI hope you don't think that saying they're precious to you here makes up for that."uMutual care doesn't erase the utility they have to you, no matter how much of a blind eye you try to turn to it."KIf you truly value them, make sure they understand it in your actions.">You have to fight for them as hard as they fight for you.""SAPHIRA: So you can't decide?" But that's not in question."So, which is it?"xSAPHIRA: Not everyone is so lucky as to be blessed with relatives who share as much compassion as they do genetics."VOr did you just choose this because you thought it was what I would want to hear?"2SAPHIRA: A new truth cannot erase an old lie."9You've chosen to prioritize me over your own values."6Is it just me, or do you treat everyone that way?"KSAPHIRA: And yet you must know the contempt your saying so will breed.">Maybe you learned your lesson, or maybe you just gave up."!Maybe there's no difference."DIn the end, you'll still have to fight just like everyone else."9Then who you are changes based on who you're facing."5What is the difference between you and a mirror?"1You have a chance to fight before you break."]SAPHIRA: Would they still be the most important to you if you were never related at all?"*SAPHIRA: And perhaps that's the case."@They're no different than your friends in that case, right?"CThey're people who you had the liberty to choose to fight for."(Not everyone is given that liberty."_SAPHIRA: Because you and them are uniquely made of something the rest of the world is not."8You fight to protect what you are, not who you are."1SAPHIRA: Freedom is air; we need it to live."4But you do not treasure the air above all else."yWe take it for granted because to do otherwise in the face of its excess would shorten our lifespans in another way."Is freedom different?"SSAPHIRA: Then, like me, you have known what it is like to be without that air."OWill there ever be a time when we do not need to grasp onto it so tightly?"=SAPHIRA: But it will not come if we do not fight for it.";SAPHIRA: Then we're the only ones prepared to survive."LIn that sense, there was no other way this tournament could have ended."6SAPHIRA: Then it should not need to be treasured."LTo prioritze freedom itself in its abudance is a symptom of indecision."GIs it a privilege or a weakness to leave that door eternally open?"5It is a privilege few may have, but none should."8Freedom of that kind is nothing short of stagnancy."*To be alive is to fight for survival."LThose who protect the privilege of stagnancy will always fail to do so."%SAPHIRA: But still you leave it."gDid you give up on yourself already, or are you just waiting for a better time to start your life?"*But nobody will wait for your answer."&There's no time like the present,"-Because there's no time but the present."3No matter how weak they are, no one is exempt."vSAPHIRA: Would you rather make a difference but be forgotten anyway, or change nothing but be remembered forever?"NSAPHIRA: Altruism is a pleasant ideal, but ideals are inherently selfish."{The only thing your answer proves is that as much as your ego needs to be stroked, it doesn't have to be others that do it."@It's even more arrogant than just wanting to be remembered.";SAPHIRA: Because in the end, what matters is your ego."GWould you presume you even know how to make a positive difference?"SAPHIRA: Positive for who?"MIdeals are inherently selfish, and nothing is without underlying values."mThe only thing you can do, no matter what you think or try, is push your own perspective onto the world."GEven children are just an opinion that has taken on its own shape."But that is the way of it."/Everyone fights for the survival of ideas."CSAPHIRA: But against all logic, your priority is still to try.":Persistence is not condemnable, but foolhardiness is."4Where among those you fall is yet to be proven."SAPHIRA: Nothing."(You got this far with no ambitions."Just for kicks?"+Entertainment is a tool for happiness."To see if you could?")Doesn't that make it about your ego?"'Maybe because of those around you?"LDid you really listen to them talk all this time without caring at all?"1To say "Nothing" is either laziness or fear."*Do you want to give that another try?"SAPHIRA: Fine."DNo matter how little it may be... what is most precious to you?"qSAPHIRA: It's only easiest to answer nothing when you're afraid of others, or of yourself knowing the truth."So which is it?"0SAPHIRA: Do you really think anybody cares?"AOr are you afraid of what you choose being used against you?"!That is not a baseless fear."?The world is out to get you, but it is not out to get YOU."ZBut even fear, that extreme way of protecting yourself, is just another way to fight."oSAPHIRA: You won't acknowledge that you care about anything, because you can't stand the pain that brings."$How badly have you been burned?"7A child learns quickly not to touch a raging fire."3It takes an adult to be willing to put it out."When will you grow up?""When will you start fighting?"No matter."%It's time for it to begin again."7SAPHIRA: Your precious thing is inside that chest.",The world does not want you to keep it."*Threats will approach from all sides."1Eliminate them before they reach their goal."Here are the rules:")If you want something, fight for it."There are no breaks."!There are no second chances."There are no other rules."Good luck."D(It is suggested to turn Speed-Up Mode off for this challenge.)"5SAPHIRA: I did say there were no second chances."'Your journey would have been over,"(But I am not as cruel as the world."(Do you need me to clarify the game?"1SAPHIRA: Do you need me to clarify the game?"1There are no second chances-- not out there."Begin.",SAPHIRA: Then learn from your mistakes."You're full of them."(And thus, you are full of strength.""Blaziken is revving up speed!",Something is lifting the treasure away!"2The chest was blown back to where it started!"#Garchomp is preparing to rush