: That's all there is.""BENNETT: I'll try running it."BENNETT: No good, then."Unfortunate."Allow me to try as well..."=For my part, I believe I'm getting closer to a solution."YI've realized that, assuming this is solvable, the logic must be ruled out in pairs."ZFor example, that large rock is blocking two of the devices in the Foliation section."~Therefore, if this is solvable, those two gems can only have Foliation that is classified as "Indistinct" or "Difficult.""ïThat much is obvious, but because there's two of those to two properties, that conversely means that the other two gems cannot have those properties."ÉAlthough we don't know for sure which gem has which property, we can rule out additional combinations by considering them together."/Perhaps that will lead us to a solution...""I'm also still working on it."dThere are some rocks in the way of the devices, but I don't think we'll be able to move them..."nI believe we're forced to assume that it is possible to solve the problem around and despite those rocks."åPerhaps they were even there when this place was more operational, but more importantly, assuming that it is impossible will get us nowhere."XThen, under that assumption, they can rule out some possibilities for us as well...":Don't worry though, I'm also working on the solution.">Keep trying, and one of us is bound to get it eventually."?BENNETT: I suppose it has been a while for you, hasn't it?"öThese machines lock a gate which can't be opened until all of the information, entered via the colored blocks lining up with the screen above, is correct."âSo if we determine that the Emerald gem had a Hardness of 6, we would move the green block directly in front of the screen that says "6"."ãWe have a set of clues from residual data, which ideally will lead us to a solution, but it will take a lot of work to piece them together."nWe can work on this together, and hopefully Victini has little further left to run by the time we finish."Shall we?"