hat's a reasonable course of thought no one could blame you for having!"PBut even I'm not dumb enough to actually blow up the train we're moving on!"âWhat if there was a chain reaction and every individual car blew up like in those movies creating a freak accident and killing everyone!?"*I'm an arsonist, not a mass-murderer!">JULIA: Okay, this is gonna sound bad, but I can explain--"During the black out..."I was..."...hiding under a table.",It's not because I was scared! Promise!"jIt's just-- I didn't expect the lights to be out for so long, I thought it would be a brief flicker--"xSo I thought, it would be funny if when the lights went out, I ducked under the table-- and then they come back on,":And then my date would be like "Huh? Where'd she go?""IAnd then I'd pop up and be like "Boo!" and I'd have totally got him!"zBut then the lights never came back up and then I thought it might be a while but I had already committed to the bit,"ÖAnd so I thought maybe the lights will stay out for a while, maybe I can just go get a snack while I'm waiting for them to come back,"äSo I crawled out and came back and then the lights turned on and now I'm under arrest, you have to help me, I just wanted to "Boo!" him!!!"IJULIA: It was Ms. Craudburry in the Ballroom with the Candlestick!!!"No, I don't know that."But that would be funny."2I don't think this train even has a ballroom."Or a candlestick."bAnyway, okay, this is going to sound really bad, but I'd rather you hear it from me than him."HMe and that guy were totally talking about how we'd rob this train."Just hypothetically!"Entirely hypothetically!"ëWe said I could go distract the conductor-- NOT blow up the engine-- and maybe turn the lights out, while he snuck into the back to nab the orbs."*But it was just for fun conversation!",We weren't going to go through with it!"2And for the record, he brought it up, not me!"2JULIA: ...Will you at least visit me in jail?"7CHIEF: This is a most lamentable turn of events..."QAfter all of our work, how could we still have failed to secure the orbs...?"'CHIEF: It's completely baffling..."FThe orbs were secured in this case, to which only I have the key."TNo one has taken the key from me, yet there's no signs of damage on the case..."*How could they have just disappeared?"And where are they now?"gCHIEF: Indeed, I was keeping a close eye on the passengers in the time leading up to the blackout."RNot too much of anything happened, but I'll tell you everything I did notice."ñThe child, Eustace, seemed to be making a fuss about everything he could-- ordering even my officers this way and that for the most trivial of things!"wI had wondered if he had been trying to occupy their attention for something-- but he is just a child after all..."/Ms. Craudburry was making a similar stink."èShe kept walking out to the center car, but as soon as she saw me, she would just yell something about the food being miserable, and head back."AI saw several others pass by, to and from the dining cart..."But thinking about it, a couple of them, such as Sandy and John, may have ended on the opposite side from where they started..."\I also noticed Julia and that gang leader consorting-- whispering a bit here and there."pI couldn't hear what they were saying, but I felt it best not to intervene in a date without more evidence."'After a time, the lights went out."VI sent my men forward just in case, and went to check on the engine room at once."$It's as you know it from there."JCHIEF: Our initial investigation has turned up six possible suspects."First, Ms. Craudburry."ZA shrewd shrew, we're aware she's engaged in illegal underground trading in the past."7Second, Sandy, the reserve Ground Type Gym Leader."äWhile it's a shame to suspect a league member, she's shown a past willingness to violate the law for admittedly well-intentioned activism."+Third, former Aqua Gang leader Archer."-Third, former Magma Gang leader Maxwell."íHis gang has been dissolved, but 