ty of this train with your PUTRESCENCE!" So much for the dining car!"iThey'd better decontaminate every square inch of this place after inviting GUTTER TRASH like YOU in!"Get away from me at once!"0My poor nose can only take so much at once."ÇCRAUDBURRY: Are you naturally this insufferable or is it just your mission to make your presence as OFFENSIVE as humanly possible?"Begone!"SANDY: Oh, hi \PN!"&Are you surprised to see me here?">It's true that I decided field work wasn't for me, but...""Desk jobs are just so boring!"MDo you know how tiring is to just sit there and organize papers all day?"eWaiting for the next Certified Cool Person to walk up and take the crazy jobs you're doling out?"3It's like-- why aren't I out there doing that?"WBut I KNOW why I'm not out there doing that-- it's because a Miltank pooped on me!"9But am I to live my life cowering in fear from one--"Heh, COW-ering..."...What was I saying?"ÖAnyway, I couldn't take the pressure of mentally ping-ponging between wanting to get outside more and wanting to hide inside forever,"\So now I'm here on a moving train going in the opposite direction from all my problems!"$Funny how life works, isn't it?"^SANDY: Hey, you don't think that there's Miltank in wherever this train is going, do you?"JOHN: \PN.""Curious to run into you here."<Rest assured, I harbor no particular resentment to you,"VEven if your actions have resulted in the deaths of several of my past employers."..."FOn second thought, I may have some slight resentment towards you,"JBut you may be relieved that I intend to deal with it professionally."Good day."JOHN: I said "Good day.""!EUSTACE: Greetings, peasant."9Make yourself useful and fetch me a drink, will you?"9Some kind of juice, I believe, would suit my palate."Be forewarned though-- present me with Leppa Juice and I shall forcibly eject you from the train while it is still moving."{Grepa Juice neither-- I don't know what else they put in that stuff, but it surely wasn't meant for human consumption."tAnd you will hold the Oran Juice as well. It is unsuitable for all occasions except the blandest of breakfasts."Hop to it, gar√ßon."FWe can't all stand around all day with stupid looks on our faces."EUSTACE: Gar√ßon?" Where is my juice, gar√ßon?"'The service here is truly abysmal."4JULIA: \PN, I thought that was you who went by!"(What a coincidence seeing you here!"JI was invited for a trip abroad by someone, and would you believe it?"I got stood up!"Me!",Imagine a cheerleader getting stood up!"RI hope the guy recently realized he was gay, or else I want an explanation!!!"xAnd if he did realize he's gay, then I hope he's very happy with his life choices and finds a wonderful husband!!!!"CBut not if the husband would've been interested in me instead!"=It's a pity-- he seemed like such a sweet-talker, too..."But no matter!"*I'm making the best of the situation!"SAnd I've met a fine gentleman in his absence, and we are having a lovely time,"+So there, Mr.Stander-Upper! Take that!"-JULIA: Maybe he just missed the train..."`I almost got on the wrong one-- but I blame him for telling me which it was so last minute!"Mrrgrgrr..."/MAXWELL: \PN. Funny running into you here."lI was just heading out on this train for a change of pace, when I met this lovely lady across from me--"JULIA: Ohstopityou~"#No, I'm kidding-- keep going--"8MAXWELL: For you, baby, I can keep going all night.".But let's take things slow, how about it?"âAnyway, regardless of whatever history we have, I do hope you wouldn't ruin a personal outing just for the sake of some petty past drama."IMy boys are back at the ranch-- you'll get no trouble from our gang."Take care."ARCHER: Ah, \PN."9I understand you're acquainted with my date tonight."ÜI was just heading out on some business-- which I would ask for your discretion with regards to, lest I mention your own involvement--"VWhen I encountered this young treasure who had been abandoned by some lesser man."EI feel it is only just not to let her mourn her rejection alone."(JULIA: Forget whoever that guy was!"!Tell me more about yourself!"(ARCHER: Naturally, all in due time."OWe have an entire voyage ahead of us to get to know each other, after all."DIn any case, I would appreciate if you granted us some privacy."NYou'll find no unsavory business from me on this ride-- you have my word.""MAXWELL: Until we meet again."%ARCHER: Some space, if you will?"KHow are we supposed to enjoy a moment between the two of us otherwise?"?MAXWELL: My date appears to have pulled a vanishing act..."ARCHER: Curious."Just where did she go...?"DMAXWELL: Well, it seems like we're on opposite sides again, hm?")But I'm innocent as innocent can be."What've you got to ask me?"JMAXWELL: You know, I don't think there's a point in denying this one."wEither of the orbs has power enough that could give me the edge I need to bring the Magma Gang back to full glory."%That's just a no-brainer, right?"II'd just be making myself look more suspicious if I lied about that.",MAXWELL: I'd love to give you an alibi."-I was sitting right here the whole time."1Didn't move an inch, like a good little boy."UThe problem is, the person who could corroborate that story disappeared herself,"1Which I'm guessing leaves me in the shitter."|She and I were having a lively conversation-- no idea why she'd just up and run off unless she got a very wrong idea..."MAXWELL: Well..."OI hate to do this, but that Julia girl said some pretty suspicious things."ÄShe suggested how she could go head up to the front and make the lights go out herself-- and then low and behold, out they went."qBut she was right here when that actually happened, so I don't imagine how she could've done that, unless...""She uses an Electrode, right?"~I'm imagining an interesting scenario in which she bowls it down the center of the train, scoring a strike in the engine room.":But I didn't see any of that, so best to discount it."6She's suspicious, but I don't think she's guilty."$MAXWELL: Good luck on this one."5ARCHER: Ah, is it my turn for the interrogation?">ARCHER: Indeed, these are the necessary questions to ask."0But you already know the answer, don't you?"hThere's no point in denying what the influence of either of those orbs could do for my former gang."=Perhaps we could finally do some good in the city again."TBut would I really have come all this way just to cling to something like that?"!Do you think so lowly of me?"IARCHER: You're right to ask, but I dreaded you doing so nonetheless."I've bided my time."PEven if I were going to steal the orbs, that was the wrong moment to do so."1Too much chaos in a darkness we didn't plan."Too many unknowns."GI sat right here and weighed my options-- but waited, nonetheless."bYou'll find me innocent, and ideally my beautiful date would have been there to back me up..."7...However it appears she's the one who's run off."DI do hope she didn't get too many ideas from our little talk..."]ARCHER: Well, I hate to do this to a lady who I was just having a wonderful time with..."3But my date did disappear during the blackout."GShe and I were having a rousing, strictly hypothetical discussion."8How would we rob this train, if we then decided to."]"If" is the key operative here-- it was a lively conversation topic; not a genuine plan."\Or so I thought, but she did mention cutting the lights-- and thus the lights were cut."cI followed through on no further part of the plan, but could she have arranged that from here?"6Without moving from her seat before the blackout?"1For an Electric Type Gym Leader... Possible."7I saw nothing, but it cannot be ruled out, can it?"ARCHER: Best of luck."On duty and reporting!"The exit is secure!"FThe chief has brought us on to make sure this ride goes smoothly.")No suspicious activity at this time!"MI caught this one sneaking up into the storage room during the blackout!"4We're gonna need you to stay right here, ma'am."WThe chief is near the front of the train, currently investigating the disturbance."SANDY: Please let me go!"8I just got lost looking for the little girl's room!"IHave you noticed that this train doesn't seem to have one anywhere?!"SANDY: Am I cursed?"Did a Hoopa jinx me?"^Is my fate to suffer misfortune after misfortune every time I so much as venture outside?"-SANDY: Don't tell me you suspect me too!"TOkay, sure, I've been known to go to extremes for the sake of the environment--"~And, sure, the Blue Orb has been said to be a powerful water source and together with the Red Orb, could reshape the climate--"àAnd... sure, the condition of the climate is a growing threat that nobody seems to either know what to do about or care enough to help--"DBut that doesn't mean I was going back there to steal the orbs!"aAlthough, if someone did steal the orbs, they should definitely use them to help the planet."*That's just a true statement of fact."Think about it?"CSANDY: Okay, so this isn't the most... positive... alibi, but."RAt the time of the incident, I was being detained by that officer over there!"EHe caught me over here-- just looking for the bathroom, I swear!"FAnd he held me up the entire time until it was already too late--"1Errr, I mean, until the lights came back on!";There's no way I could've had a chance to go get them!"SANDY: I'm glad you asked!"BYou remember that Ignosia Craudburry whose office we flooded?"9Turns out she's here, and I think she wants revenge!"sShe started working from home after that, and I mayyy have intercepted some of her personal correspondences..."8She wants to sell the orbs to her corporate shills!"$You know that Craudburry woman?"zI happened to come into some information when looking around at her role in the city, and I think she wants the orbs!"9Something about selling them off for corporate use--"JShe has a history of illegal trading, and this is right up her alley!"UAnd who knows what she'd buy with all the money she could get from selling them!"#Don't trust anything she says!"SANDY: Save me!"JOHN: Agh!"What do you want?!"'JOHN: Motives?! Motives for what?!"{What motive could I possibly have to steal the Red and Blue Orbs and use them to return Team Meteor to their former might?!"7JOHN: Pshh-- I need no alibi, for I am innocent..."Ü...And because although I confess, I may have charged towards the storage car with the intent of stealing just a glance at the orbs..."%I was assailed in the darkness--"By all of these boxes...",I tripped on one, stumbled back here..."_Passed out, and then when the lights were back on, I thought it wisest to remain hidden..."...It was not wise."I may have hit my head..."JOHN: Hmph..."vI haven't seen much of the others-- except for stepping on that boy as he was hollering about something or other."bI swear, that child screamed louder than some of our toughest cases at Dr. Connal's clinic..."...Eustace, his name was?"`I believe I saw that screen name in the CC of the message I received about this train ride.")"EustaceOverlord," I believe it was."=What a devil child. He was certainly planning something."jBut I suspect several others of the notable passengers on this train received the same message I did.":The orbs were aboard-- they could be stolen, it said.">There were five recipients of the message besides myself."ESomeone was clearly setting all of this up, but who could it be?"%JOHN: Yes, allow me a respite..."My head still aches..."ÜEUSTACE: If you don't let me off this train right now, I swear on your mother's life I will sue you to the ends of the world and back."/This is a violation of my rights, officer."JYou are keeping me here unlawfully and you will lose your job for it,">And subsequently, your home-- your family-- your friends,"ÑEverything you know and have will be decimated all because of your one foolish arbitrary mistake to confine me here against my will."Now let me go, officer."GK-kid please, I've been ordered not to let anyone leave the train."8That's my job, there's nothing unlawful about it..."...Right?"fI can confidently say that no person has left or boarded the train since we departed the station!"9Whoever the culprit is, they must still be on board!"'...Not for lack of trying, though."JAs soon as the lights went out, that kid over there wouldn't shut up."OHe kept screaming the entire time as if he were in some kind of mad panic."1At least we know he didn't leave the room..."6The chief is investigating the disturbance ahead."KPlease do not disturb him unless you have something to report as well."BCONDUCTOR: The Red Orb was buried in the devastated engine..."NThere's a cavity where it could fit-- but how could it have gotten there?"UI was in the room the whole time, though the cavity was obstructed from my view."I just don't understand..."^CONDUCTOR: I'm not sure what's going on, but if you can help it, please don't drip on me?"CRAUDBURRY: INCOMPETENTS!"+Can't even drive a simple train right!"How do you mess that up!?"3It only goes in a predetermined straight line!"QBut then drunkard fools can't even do that much-- is that what they all are?"åBLATHERING IDIOTS probably can't so much as leave their front door without tripping down the stairs and slamming their head on the pavement!"PProbably explains the BRAIN DAMAGE necessary to fail at such a simple task."RDoes old Craudburry need to come in there and show you morons how it's done?!"åRoll up my sleeves and press the shiny green 'GO' button for you since APPARENTLY that's too much for you primitive MEATSACKS to comprehend!"8CONDUCTOR: Goodness, I barely know what happened...":But if I can help in any way, I'm happy to cooperate."NCONDUCTOR: We're currently a short distance north of the 1R253 Scrapyard."JTechnically, we've left the Reborn region, but we haven't gotten far."pThe area we're in is called the Greater Tourmaline Desert-- it's a wasteland of sandstorms and nothingness."vTravelling on foot in this area is usually impossible, unlike the inner Tourmaline area within the Reborn region."DHere, the distance is too great, and the sandstorms too fierce."There's nothing for miles."YThey always told us about how more and more accidents happen around the Scrapyard...",It seems we'll be counted among them..."CONDUCTOR: I'm doing the best I can, and we at least got power restored to the cars, but I'm afraid the engine is a goner."wWe're completely grounded, and I suspect no repairs short of a completely new engine car are going to change that."RFortunately, the comm system is intact, and we've been able to radio for aid."8A rescue train is departing from Grandview Station."IWe'll load up the passengers and crew, and get everyone home safely."8But until it arrives, we've nothing to do but wait."IFor better or worse, that likely holds true for the culprit as well."4They're trapped here just as much as any of us."ÜCONDUCTOR: My attention was squarely on the controls the entire time before the incident-- but I'm afraid I barely know what happened.";The entire car went dark, and I heard a strange noise."PIt sounded like a Pok√©mon's attack-- but not one I've ever heard before..."+Reflexively, I slammed on the brakes--">Or more like I hit them in a panic, but good thing I did!"^The train came to a stop just as the engine began to make all kinds of unpleasant noises."Fearing the worst, I took cover in the back landing just in time to see shards of metal and glass fly forward with a boom."{Once the train and the sounds both came to a stop, I was able to restore power quickly, and the room was as you saw it now."lI'll continue searching to see if I can find out any more about the cause of the engine failure though."CONDUCTOR: Just as well."Good luck out there."GCHIEF: Great galloping Golisopods... How could this have happened?"Oh, \PN!"3I swear, you scared the daylights out of me..."Tell me the orbs are safe!".". ."
