shes the target by rolling over it. This may also make the target flinch."hThe user bites the target. If the target is holding a Berry, the user eats it and gains its effect."aThe user attacks with powdery scales blown by the wind. This may raise all the user's stats."hWhile resisting, the user attacks the opposing Pok√©mon. This lowers the Sp. Atk stat of those hit."fThe user attacks twice in succession by jabbing with two spikes. This may also poison the target."mThe target is slashed with scythes or claws. This attack becomes more powerful if it hits in succession."jThe user drains the target's blood. The user's HP is restored by half the damage taken by the target."bSharp spikes are shot at the target in rapid succession. They hit two to five times in a row."gThe user calls out their underlings to shield their body, raising their Defense and Sp. Def stats."cThe user calls out their underlings to heal them. The user regains up to half of their max HP."kThe user performs a beautiful, mystic dance. This boosts the user's Sp. Atk, Sp. Def, and Speed stats."fThe user scatters a cloud of irritating powder to draw attention. Opponents aim only at the user."UThe user ensnares the target with thin, gooey silk so it can't flee from battle."nThe opposing Pok√©mon are bound with silk blown from the user's mouth that harshly lowers the Speed stat."dThe user stares at flashing lights to focus their mind, drastically raising their Sp. Atk stat."eTurns the target's power against it. The higher the target's Attack stat, the greater the power."fThe user lets loose a pitch-black shock wave at the target. This may lower the target's Accuracy."eThe user crunches up the target with sharp fangs. This may also lower the target's Defense stat."gThe user releases a horrible aura imbued with dark thoughts. This may also make the target flinch."hThis move enables the user to attack first. It fails if the target is not readying a damaging move."cThe user slashes the target the instant an op