hen strikes on the next turn. It strikes even if the target protects itself."iThe user befriends the target, making it lose the will to fight. It lowers the target's Attack stat."gThe user plays rough with the target and attacks it. This may also lower the target's Attack stat."gThe user covers the target in combustible powder. It explodes if the target uses a Fire-type move."cStriking opponents over and over hardens the user's fists. This raises the user's Attack stat."dTilling the soil, the user raises the Attack and Sp. Atk stats of grounded Grass-type Pok√©mon."dProtecting the user from attacks, this move also damages any attacker who makes direct contact."fThe user weaves a sticky net, lowering the Speed stat of opposing Pok√©mon switching into battle."fAll stat changes affecting the target turn topsy-turvy and become the opposite of what they were."ZThe user takes the target trick-or-treating. This changes the target's type to Ghost."nWith an odd poisonous liquid, the user lowers the Attack, Sp. Atk, and Speed stats of poisoned opponents."bThe user attacks with throwing stars two to five times in a row. This move always goes first."LA unique attack that varies in type depending on the Pok√©mon using it."LA unique attack that varies in type depending on the Pok√©mon using it."LA unique attack that varies in type depending on the Pok√©mon using it."LA unique attack that varies in type depending on the Pok√©mon using it."LA unique attack that varies in type depending on the Pok√©mon using it."LA unique attack that varies in type depending on the Pok√©mon using it."LA unique attack that varies in type depending on the Pok√©mon using it."LA unique attack that varies in type depending on the Pok√©mon using it."LA unique attack that varies in type depending on the Pok√©mon using it."LA unique attack that varies in type depending on the Pok√©mon using it."LA unique attack that varies in type depending on the Pok√©mon using it."LA unique attack that varies in type depe