s their body around violently to inflict damage on everything in their vicinity."aThe user burns themselves out for massive damage. The user then will no longer be Fire-type."iThe user rubs the scales on their body, making a huge noise. It then lowers the user's Defense stat."gA damaging move that also eliminates the targets' Abilities if they have already used their moves."hThe user swings both arms and strikes. The target's stat changes don't affect this attack's damage."TThe user uses their body like a hammer to attack the target and inflict damage."aThe user strikes the target with a burning lash. This also lowers the target's Defense stat."\Although this move has great power, it only works the first turn the user is in battle."bThe user unleashes a strong beam. The attack's recoil harshly lowers the user's Sp. Atk stat."gThe user restores the target's HP by up to half of its max HP. Restores more HP on Grassy Terrain."iThe user engages their gears to raise Attack and Sp. Atk stats of allies with Plus or Minus Ability."BThe user fiercely attacks the target using their entire body."aThe user swings and hits with their strong, heavy fist. It lowers the user's Speed, however."GThe user instructs the target to use the target's last move again."eBy concentrating intensely, the user's attack on the next turn always results in a critical hit."8The user attacks by pelting the target with leaves."jThe user slams the target with a full-force water blast. It may lower the Defense stat of the target."^The user lunges at the target with full force. This also lowers the target's Attack stat."YThe user emits a sinister ray to attack. This move will ignore the target's Ability."RThe user hits the target with the force of nature. It halves the target's HP."iThe user attacks with a pollen puff that explodes. If the target is an ally, it restores HP instead."mThe user boasts their strength and strikes. The more the user's stats are raised, the greater the power."fThe user shoots powerful lasers using the power of a prism. The user can't move on the next turn."iThe user bites the target with psychic capabilities. This can also destroy Light Screen and Reflect."dSummoning psychic energies, the user turns the battlefield into Psychic Terrain for five turns."VThe user heals the target's status condition. It also restores the user's own HP."hThe user attacks the target by dancing very hard. The user's type determines the type of this move."dThe user beats the target with a bone containing a spirit. This may lower the target's Defense."qThe user sets a shell trap. If the user is hit by a physical move, the trap will explode and inflict damage."UThe user regains up to half of their max HP. It restores more HP in a sandstorm."KThe user stabs the target with a sharp horn. This attack never misses."_The user fills a blade with light energy on the first turn, then attacks on the next turn."iThe user bursts into song, emitting many bubbles. If any target had a burn, the burn will be lifted."^The user hides in the target's shadow, steals the target's stat boosts, and then attacks."4The user exchanges Speed stats with the target."eThe user attacks while stitching the target's shadow to the ground, preventing it from escaping."`The user shines a spotlight on the target so that only it will be attacked during the turn."qDriven by frustration, the user attacks. If the user's previous move failed, the power of this move doubles."eThe user restores HP equal to the target's Attack stat. It also lowers the target's Attack stat."kThe user slams into the target with the force of a meteor. This move will ignore the target's Ability."dTeary eyes make the target lose the desire to fight. It lowers the target's Attack and Sp. Atk."aThe user attacks the target's throat. The target cannot use sound-based moves for two turns."^The user shoots poisonous threads to poison the target and lower the target's Speed stat."cThe user lands an intense kick of tropical origins. Thi